; MI Systems  MI-CACHE  Disk Caching Utility Version 1.0
; Copyright (C) 1992. All rights reserved.
;
;
; TECHNICAL NOTES
;
;
; Hard Disk BIOS
;
; It turns out that the reason the cache wont work on a hard disk is because the
; HD BIOS is more intelligent than I first thought. You can ask the HD BIOS for any
; number of sectors up to 80H, so an overrun will occur when you add the first sector
; number to the number of sectors-1.
; So now when we have a call to our INT13 with the number of sectors out of range, we must
; deal with it properly. For efficiency's sake we must still call the old handler with
; the same number of sectors, but they must be stored in the cache in n-sector tracks.
; ie. if we read fs=1 and ns=34 (on 17 spt)
;
;
; Extended 1
;
; When we want to use Extended/Expanded memory then there is a buffering problem in how
; we transfer the data from the disk via the cache to memory. If the data is not in the
; cache then we must read it into the cache. At present we read the disk into the cache,
; and then read from the cache into memory. However, if the cache has been set up in
; extended memory then this cannot be done. Thus on reading we must read from the disk
; straight into memory (if not in cache) and then copy it back into the cache from memory.
; This would seem easy enough, except when we get the case where we have part of the track
; in the cache already and we need to read some more of that track from the disk into
; the cache to make the CT entry valid. In this case we might not be reading data from the
; disk which will be going into memory:
;  Eg.   1  2  3  4  5  6  7  8  9
;        X  X  X  X                  - in cache
;                          R  R  R   - required
;  Here we would read sectors 5 through to 9, but only 7-9 are to be put in memory.
; The first solution is to set up a temporary track in conventional memory which can be
; used as a buffer in this circumstance, but we would still read from disk->memory->cache
; mainly. Alternatively, if this situation occurs then we read only those sectors we
; require (7-9) and mark the CT as only having those sectors, then we can read straight
; into memory (using the memory as a buffer).
;  The temp. track would be the maximum possible and would normally be 512*18 = 9K, but
; could be 1024*18 = 18K or 512*33 = 15K for different disks.
;  The rereading would mean we would lose previously read information and decrease caching
; performance, but requires no extra memory. In fact it would be better to completely
; invalidate the track so that we have to read from disk anyway. Thus: if we have the track
; in the cache, but it does not have all the required sectors and those sectors we must
; read extra are all requested then read sectors via memory as buffer, else invalidate CT.
;
;
; Extended 2
;
; When we allocate extended memory we cannot do as I first thought and allocate one CT
; seperately from the XMM. This is because there are a limited number of handles available
; and thus we should be nice and use up one handle. There for we must check that the
; largest available block will meet our requirements and allocate that. CTsegD will then
; have a half-kilobyte offset into the extended block (0-32GB).
;
;
; Expanded 1
;
; We basically have the same problem as extended in that CTsegD must contain a half-kb
; offset into the mapping via the handle. We have to first load the CT that we require
; into the physical page, calculate the correct offset in the emmsegD and then perform
; our memory tasks.
;
;
; Stack
;
; Due to expanded memory it is recommended that we have our own substantial stack, the
; actual size of which is yet unknown - 512 for now.
;
;
; Saving and Restoring State
;
; It has become necessary as we use the different memory type to save and restore the state
; of the system as we enter the INT13 isr. Apart from switching to an internal stack, we
; also save the state of the A20 line for extended, and the mapping context for expanded.
; However, if the program fails for some reason, eg. critical disk error, then we must be
; able to restore the state and stabilise the cache. To to this its probably best to catch
; the INT24 interrupt and on an error we can restore properly, also to null the CTRL-C
; vector so that it will never bother us.
;
;
; 386 Enhancements
;
; If the machine is a 386+ then we are allowed to use another string movement function
; ie. MOVS DIR, which will increase the speed of block transfers within the caching.
; Therefore at startup of the cache we check to see whether the processor if a 386+ and
; set an internal flag. From then on, any block movements within the caching routines
; will use the faster DWORD versions.
; NOTE: to assemble the code we require MIL version 1.2+, and MASM version 5.1+
;
;
; UMB 1
;
; The memory allocation of the UBMs doesn't seem to work with the documented XMS
; calls, as it always returns 'UMBs unavailable' if the UMBs are there, and 'funtion
; not implemented if there aren't. Therefore we have to use the standard DOS calls
; to alter the memory allocation and link strategies to be able to allocate a UMB.
; At present there is no other checking of the UBMs presence except in error conditions
; returned by these functions. If we are certain that they do not exist below DOS 5.0
; then we should add this check. UMBs will only exist on the 286+, but we shouldn't really
; concern ourselves with this.
;
;
; UMB 2
;
; If UMBs do exists then we might as well take full use of them. The ways in which we
; can do this are as follows:
;  1) We can put the CT descriptors in a UMB to save on conventional memory.
;  2) If we are not using CONVENTIONAL we can place the temporary track in UMB memory.
; The best way to do this is probably to detect whether UMBs exist, and if they do then
; we can try and use them to their full extent.
;
;
; Memory for CT Descriptors (and temporary track)
;
; I think it would be a good idea to allocate the memory via DOS for the temporary track
; and the CT descriptors. This is so that our cache program will always be less than is
; required to load the memory image on executing. With the code to access the track and
; descriptors being written for 'not knowing where they are' we could then quite easily
; implement UMB support (see above) for these extra items.
;
;
; IBM Interrupt Chaining Protocol
;
; There exists a protocol for interrupt chaining so that such handlers can quite easily
; be removed from the chain. At the start of the interrupt handler there exists an 18
; byte header containing information about the handler.
;   00 JMP SHORT to start of handler
;   02 Previous Interrupt Handler
;   06 Signature word (424BH)
;   08 Flags - normally 0, 80H if first handler (h/w)
;   09 JMP SHORT Reset - handler h/w reset, else point to RETF
;   0B Reserved (0) - 7 bytes
;
;
; Parameters:
;
;  If Not Resident:
; Done   -?     Help
; Done   -X     Use Extended memory (abort if doesn't exist or less than 64K, else use all)
; Done   -E     Use Expanded memory
; Done   -C     Use conventional memory
; Done           If no memory type defined, try X,E and C
;
; Done   -A     Allow redundant writes
; Done   -D     Start up cache disabled
; Done   -H     Show hit indicator
;        -M     Minimise conventional memory
; Done   -R     Give read priority over writes (if sector in cache was writen to disk
;               then if reading, read from the disk and ignore the cache)
; Done   -T:nn  Read ahead by nn sectors in track (if nn is spt then 'read rest of track')
;
;  If Resident:
; Done   -?     Help
; Done   -D     Disable cache
; Done   -E     Enable cache
; Done   -F     Flush cache
;        -M     Display measurements
;        -O     Show options
; Done   -U     Unload
;
;
DVERSION EQU 0
#IF DVERSION
DEBUG   EQU 1
NOWRITE EQU 1
#ELSE
DEBUG EQU 0
NOWRITE EQU 0
#ENDIF
;
; Memory types
MEMUNDEFINED EQU 0
CONVENTIONAL EQU 1
EXTENDED     EQU 2
EXPANDED     EQU 3

; Header for each Cache Track
STRUCT CACHETRACK {
   WORD CTmruD	; next CT in list
   WORD CTlruD	; previous CT
   WORD CTsegD	; seg address of CTDATA
   ;
   BYTE CTdrive	; drive (0,1..80..) for CT
   WORD CTtrackD	; 10bit track number
   BYTE CThead	; head number
   BYTE CTfsector	; first sector number in CT
   BYTE CTsectors	; number of sectors in CT
   BYTE CTlocked	; if 1 locks CT in cache
   BYTE CTlastop	; 0=undefined,2=read,3=write
   LIST CTblank (2)
}

; There will be an array of 4 of these structures for the drives
; A(00), B(01), C(80), D(81). If we are to exclude the drive from the
; cache then we mark the type as 0. If the drive is invalid (not found) we mark
; the type as 0. If it is a hard disk, we load the boot sector and read the
; number of spt and store it in DRVspt. For floppy disks with change detection
; we will re-assign the spt value when we read in the boot sector for the first
; time. If the drive has no change detection, then we assume 8 and for sectors
; over this, just read/write them stright to disk
;
STRUCT DRIVEDEF {
   BYTE DRVid	; drive number
   BYTE DRVtype	; type of drive: (0=not used, 1=no change,
	; 2=change, 3=hard disk)
   BYTE DRVspt	; SpT for this drive (or disk if floppy)
   BYTE DRVheads
   WORD DRVbpsD	; Bps for drive
}

STRUCT XMDEF {
   LIST XMlen (4)
   WORD XMhsourceD
   LIST XMsource (4)
   WORD XMhdestD
   LIST XMdest (4)
}

;------------------------
DECLARE (DATA)
DECLARE (CODE)
;------------------------
main ()
{
JMP begin
;------------------------

; stack
LIST mystack (512)

; Process information
WORD pspD	; program segment prefix
WORD dosversionD	; MSDOS version number
WORD datasegD	; segment of our DS
BYTE is386	; set if 386 processor

; Memory management
BYTE memorytype	; Extended, Expanded, conventional
WORD requestedKD	; cache size in K
WORD oldssD
WORD oldspD
; extended
BYTE a20state	; saved state of A20 line
LIST xms (4)	; XMS entry point
WORD xmmhandleD	; handle for XMM block
LIST xmsblock (XMDEF)
; expanded
WORD emmsegD	; page segment for EMM
WORD emmhandleD	; handle to pages
; ubms
BYTE umbs	; umb? 0=none,ff=yes, but we dont use them
	;      1=for CT, 2=for temptrack

; Disk management
BYTE errorcode	; disk read/write error
BYTE dosdrive	; drive number via DOS
BYTE drive	; drive number for INT13
WORD disk_bpsD	; bps for current disk
BYTE disk_spt	; spt for current disk
WORD max_bpsD	; max bps for any disk
WORD max_sptD	; max spt for any disk
BYTE disk_heads	; number disk heads for current disk
BYTE int13_operation	; current INT13 operation
BYTE int13_drive	; current INT13 paramters
BYTE int13_head
BYTE int13_sectors
BYTE int13_fsector
WORD int13_trackD
LIST int13_buffer (4)
BYTE newfs
BYTE newns
LIST drivetable (DRIVEDEF*4)	; drive table

; Cache management
WORD tracksegD	; segment addres of temp track
WORD cachesegD	; segment address of cache
WORD number_ctsD	; number of CT entries
WORD ct_lengthD	; length of one CT track table
WORD ct_lengthinparasD	; length of CT track table in paras
WORD ct_lruD	; offset of LRU CT
WORD ct_mruD	; offset of MRU CT
BYTE aicount	; flag for AI read ahead
WORD aitrackD
BYTE aihead
BYTE aidrive
BYTE moretodo
BYTE cacheoff
BYTE floppy0ok
BYTE floppy1ok

; measurements
LIST logicals (4)	; number logical transfers
LIST physicals (4)	; number physical transfers
WORD convusedD	; conventional memory used

; options
BYTE allowredundant	; ignore redundant writes
BYTE hitindicator	; show hit indicator
BYTE minimise	; minimise conventional memory
BYTE readpriority	; give read priority
BYTE restoftrack	; flag for 'read rest of track'
BYTE readahead	; readahead count
#IF DVERSION
BYTE allowwrite
#ENDIF
;
BYTE uninstall	; uninstall flag
BYTE displaycache	; displayflag
BYTE showparas	; show options used
BYTE showmeasures	; show performance
BYTE disable	; disable cache
BYTE rflush	; ask to flush the cache

; misc
WORD axtempD	; temp store for AX
WORD retaddrD	; temp return address
BYTE installed	; if we are or not
WORD displayparaD	; video
WORD oldhitD

; debug
#IF DEBUG ;===
MESSAGE otherop = 'Other operation '
MESSAGE readop = 'Read...'
MESSAGE writeop = 'Write...'
MESSAGE incache = 'Cached...'
MESSAGE readnocache = 'No cache...'
MESSAGE flshcache = 'Flush...'
MESSAGE cacheok = 'Cache Ok'
MESSAGE cacheused = 'Cache used'
MESSAGE cachenotused = 'Cache not used'
MESSAGE diskerror = 'Disk error'
MESSAGE aiguess = 'AI used...'
MESSAGE wrongdrive = 'Wrong drive...'
MESSAGE readextra = 'EXTRA...'
MESSAGE out13 = 'Exit 13'
MESSAGE pre13 = 'Pre 13'
MESSAGE floppy = 'Floppy boot sector..'
BYTE keepfailing

LIST gnum (6)
MESSAGE spaces = '   '

LIST testsector (2048)
#ENDIF ;======
;------------------------
LABEL begin

AX = CS
DS = AX

CLI
;AX = &initstack
MOV AX,OFFSET initstack
AX += 15
CX = 16
XOR DX,DX
DIV CX
CX = CS
AX += CX
SS = AX
AX = 250
SP = AX
STI

init()	; get psp,memory,commandtail,etc
IF (NC)
   ; failed to initialise
   AX = 4C01H
   INT 21H
ENDIF

AX = 4C00H
INT 21H
}
;------------------------
myINT13 ()
FAR
{
; We will use the IBM Interrupt Chaining Protocol
; which defines a header in the format:
;   00 JMP SHORT overheader
;   02 old interupt vector
;   06 signature (424BH)
;   08 flags (00 - 80H for first handler)
;   09 JMP SHORT reset - for h/w - just point to RETF
;   0B Reserved (0) - 7 bytes
;   22

JMP SHORT int13begin
LIST normINT13 (4)
DW 424BH
DB 0
JMP SHORT int13ret
DB 7 DUP (0)
LABEL int13ret
RETF

LABEL int13begin

; Our Disk BIOS routine
;
; AH = 2 (read) AH = 3 (write)
; AL = number sectors
; CL = sector number (plus 2 bits of track number)
; CH = track number
; DL = drive number
; DH = head number
;
CLI
PUSH DS
PUSH AX
AX = datasegD
DS = AX
POP AX
DO
   #IF DVERSION
   IF (allowwrite = 0)
   #IF DEBUG
   #IF NOWRITE
   IF (AH = 3 || AH = 0BH)
      AH = 3
      POP DS
      STC
      STI
      RET 2
   ENDIF
   #ENDIF
   #ENDIF
   ENDIF
   #ENDIF
   ;
   DO
      EXITL (AH <> 0FFH)
      EXITL (CL <> 'M' || CH <> 'I')
      IF (AL = 0)
         ; check installation?
         POP DS
         CL = 'O'
         CH = 'k'
         AH = cacheoff
         CLC
         STI
         RET 2
      ENDIF
      IF (AL = 1)
         ; uninstalling?
         uninstall_tsr()
         AX = 0
         CMC
         IF (NC)
            AL = 'O'
            AH = 'k'
         ENDIF
         POP DS
         STI
         RET 2
      ENDIF
      #IF DEBUG ;===
      IF (AL = 2)
         ; displaying?
         dodisplaycache()
         CLC
         POP DS
         STI
         RET 2
      ENDIF
      #ENDIF ;======
      IF (AL = 3)
         ; disabling or enabling, first must flush cache
         IF (DL = 0)
            cacheoff = 1
         ELSE
            cacheoff = 0
         ENDIF
         flush_cache(0FFH)
         CLC
         POP DS
         STI
         RET 2
      ENDIF
      IF (AL = 4)
         ; request to flush cache
         flush_cache(0FFH)
         CLC
         POP DS
         STI
         RET 2
      ENDIF
      IF (AL = 5)
         ; request measurement data
         AX = CS
         ES = AX
         BX = &logicals
         DX = requestedKD
         AL = memorytype
         CLC
         POP DS
         STI
         RET 2
      ENDIF
      IF (AL = 6)
         ; request parameter data
         AX = CS
         ES = AX
         BX = &allowredundant
         AL = memorytype
         CLC
         POP DS
         STI
         RET 2
      ENDIF
   END
   ; see if we support the drive
   IF (cacheoff = 0)
      PUSH AX
      testdrive(DL)
      POP AX
      IF (C) ; drive ok
         ; but we can only split a request into tracks once we know the
         ; geometry, which for a floppy comes from its boot sector, so
         ; until then the only request we take is a read of that sector
         PUSH AX
         geometryknown(DL)
         POP AX
         EXIT (C)
         EXIT (AH = 2 && AL = 1 && CX = 1 && DH = 0)
      ENDIF
   ENDIF
   ; call the old BIOS
   POP DS
   #IF DEBUG
   PUSHF
   PUSH AX
   PUSH BX
   PUSH CX
   PUSH DX
   PUSH DI
   PUSH SI
   PUSH DS
   PUSH ES
   PUSH AX
   AX = CS
   DS = AX
   POP AX
   debugregs()
   POP ES
   POP DS
   POP SI
   POP DI
   POP DX
   POP CX
   POP BX
   POP AX
   POPF
   #ENDIF
   CLI
   PUSHF
   CALL DWORD PTR normINT13
   STI
   #IF DEBUG
   PUSHF
   PUSH AX
   PUSH BX
   PUSH DS
   PUSH ES
   AX = CS
   DS = AX
   debugline(&out13,1)
   POP ES
   POP DS
   POP BX
   POP AX
   POPF
   #ENDIF
   RET 2
END

; we do support the drive
errorcode = 0
DO
   EXITL (AH <> 2 && AH <> 3)
   ;
   ; swap to our own internal stack
   CLI
   axtempD = AX
   AX = SP
   oldspD = AX
   AX = SS
   oldssD = AX
   AX = &mystack
   AX += 508
   SP = AX
   AX = CS
   SS = AX
   AX = axtempD
   ;
   ; read/write operation
   int13_operation = AH
   int13_sectors = AL
   pushall()
   ;
   int13_drive = DL
   int13_head = DH
   int13_buffer.0.D = BX
   int13_buffer.2.D = ES
   AL = CL
   AND CL,00111111B
   int13_fsector = CL
   AH = 0
   SHL AX,1
   SHL AX,1
   AL = CH
   int13_trackD = AX
   ;
   #IF DEBUG
   PUSH AX
   PUSH DX
   displayinfo()
   POP DX
   POP AX
   #ENDIF
   ;
   ; check if we are out of bounds
   moretodo = 0
   CL = int13_fsector
   CH = int13_sectors
   AL = CL
   AL += CH
   AL--
   AH = 0
   BL = disk_spt
   DIV BL
   ; if AL = 0            - one track upto sector AL
   ; If AL = 1 && AH = 0  - read to end of this track (ie. upto spt)
   ; if AL = 1 && AH = <> 0 - read rest of track and AL sectors in next track
   DO
      EXIT (AL = 0)
      EXIT (AL = 1 && AH = 0)
      ; now AL >= 1
      IF (AH = 0)
         AL--
      ENDIF
      moretodo = AL ; tracks after this one
      CL = int13_fsector
      AL = disk_spt - CL
      AL++
      CH = AL
   END
   newfs = CL
   newns = CH
   int13_sectors -= CH
   ;
   savestate()
   ;
   logicals.0.D += 1
   IF (C)
      logicals.2.D += 1
   ENDIF
   ;
   DO
      IFL (int13_operation = 2)
         #IF DEBUG ;===
         PUSH AX
         debugline(&readop,0)
         POP AX
         #ENDIF ;======
         scan_cache_for_sector()
         ; returns C (in cache) and AX (CT entry), DX (offset of first sector)
         ; else NC (not in cache)
         IF (NC) ; not in cache
            #IF DEBUG ;===
            PUSH AX
            debugline(&readnocache,0)
            POP AX
            #ENDIF ;======
            read_into_cache() ; returns DX with offset of sector, AX with CT
            EXITL (errorcode <> 0) ; disk error
            IF (AX = 0FFFFH) ; all CTs are locked, read from disk
               JMP exit13normal
            ENDIF
         ENDIF
         ; sector is in cache: AX (CT), DX (sector offset in cache)
         #IF DEBUG ;===
         PUSH AX
         debugline(&incache,0)
         POP AX
         #ENDIF ;======
         IF (hitindicator = 1)
            sethit()
         ENDIF
         read_from_cache(AX,DX)
         EXITL (errorcode <> 0)
         ;
         ; see if there are more
         check_for_more() ; returns C if more, and has updated variables
         CONTINUE (C)
         ; no more
         #IF DEBUG ;===
         PUSH AX
         debugline(&cacheok,1)
         POP AX
         #ENDIF ;======
         JMP exit13normal
      ENDIF
      ;
      IFL (int13_operation = 3)
         #IF DEBUG ;===
         PUSH AX
         debugline(&writeop,0)
         POP AX
         #ENDIF ;======
         scan_cache_for_sector()
         ; returns C (in cache) and AX (CT entry), DX (offset of first sector)
         ; else NC (not in cache)
         IF (C) ; in cache
            #IF DEBUG ;===
            PUSH AX
            debugline(&incache,0)
            POP AX
            #ENDIF ;======
            PUSH AX ; save CT
            compare_cache(AX) ; compares memory with cache
            POP AX
            IF (C)
               ; compare ok
               ;
               ; check for more
               IF (hitindicator = 1)
                  sethit()
               ENDIF
               check_for_more()
               CONTINUEL (C)
               ; set for done
               ; AL = sectors transferred
               ; AH = 0
               ; NC
               #IF DEBUG ;===
               PUSH AX
               debugline(&cacheused,1)
               POP AX
               #ENDIF ;======
               JMP exit13normal
            ENDIF
            ; else memory is different, so reload cache track
            ; we want to reuse the CT in AX
         ELSE
            DI = ct_lruD ; use LRU CT
            AX = cachesegD
            ES = AX
            ; find next unlocked CT
            REPEAT
               EXIT (ES.DI.CTlocked = 0)
               DI = ES.DI.CTmruD.D
               EXIT (DI = 0FFFFH)
            ENDREP
            AX = DI
         ENDIF
         ; sector is not in cache
         ; use CT in AX (CT)
         PUSH AX
         write_to_disk () ; write out INT13 call to disk
         POP AX
         EXIT (errorcode <> 0) ; disk error
         IF (AX <> 0FFFFH)
            ; all CTs are not locked
            write_to_cache(AX) ; copy memory into the cache
         ENDIF
         ;
         ; more?
         check_for_more()
         CONTINUEL (C)
         ;
         ; set for done
         ; AL = sectors transferred
         ; AH = 0
         ; NC
         #IF DEBUG ;===
         PUSH AX
         debugline(&cachenotused,1)
         POP AX
         #ENDIF ;======
         JMP exit13normal
      ENDIF
   END
   ; error in disk IO
   #IF DEBUG
   PUSH AX
   debugline(&diskerror,1)
   POP AX
   #ENDIF
   IF (hitindicator = 1)
      clearhit()
   ENDIF
   restorestate()
   popall()
   ; switch back to our old stack
   CLI
   axtempD = AX
   AX = oldspD
   SP = AX
   AX = oldssD
   SS = AX
   AX = axtempD
   STI
   ;
   POP DS
   AH = errorcode
   AL = 0
   STC
   STI
   RET 2
END
DO
   EXIT (AH <> 16H)
   ; intercept the change disk status call
   ; first call the old handler
   POP DS
   CLI
   PUSHF
   CALL DWORD PTR normINT13
   ; examine the change flag
   PUSHF
   IF (AH = 6) ; disk has changed
       PUSH DS
       PUSH AX
       AX = datasegD
       DS = AX
       POP AX
       pushall()
       ;
       #IF DEBUG
       PUSH AX
       debugline(&flshcache,0)
       POP AX
       #ENDIF
       flush_cache(DL)
       ;
       popall()
       POP DS
   ENDIF
   POPF
   STI
   RET 2
END
; other operation which we are not concerned with
#IF DEBUG ;===
pushall()
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
AL = AH
AH = 0
numasc(BX,AX)
debugline(&otherop,0)
debugline(&gnum,1)
popall()
#ENDIF ;======
POP DS
CLI
PUSHF
CALL DWORD PTR normINT13
STI
RET 2

LABEL exit13normal
;
IF (hitindicator = 1)
   clearhit()
ENDIF
restorestate()
popall()
; switch back to our old stack
CLI
axtempD = AX
AX = oldspD
SP = AX
AX = oldssD
SS = AX
AX = axtempD
STI
;
POP DS
AH = 0
CLC
STI
RET 2

}
;------------------------
#IF DEBUG ;===
debugline (dlineD,dnl)
WORD
BYTE
{
SAVE BX,CX
BX = dlineD
CL = BX.0
CH = 0
BX++
DO
   EXIT (CL = 0)
   AL = BX.0
   BX++
   EXIT (AL = 0)
   debugchar(AL)
   LOOP
END
IF (dnl = 1)
   debugchar(10)
   debugchar(13)
ENDIF
}
;------------------------
debugchar (dchar)
BYTE
{
SAVE BX,DX,ES
AH = 0EH
AL = dchar
INT 10H
}
;------------------------
debugregs()
{
PUSH BX
PUSH AX
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
POP AX
numasc(BX,AX)
debugline(&gnum,0)
debugline(&spaces,0)
;
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
POP AX
numasc(BX,AX)
debugline(&gnum,0)
debugline(&spaces,0)
;
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
numasc(BX,CX)
debugline(&gnum,0)
debugline(&spaces,0)
;
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
numasc(BX,DX)
debugline(&gnum,0)
debugline(&spaces,0)
;
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
numasc(BX,DI)
debugline(&gnum,0)
debugline(&spaces,0)
;
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
numasc(BX,SI)
debugline(&gnum,0)
debugline(&spaces,0)
;
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
numasc(BX,ES)
debugline(&gnum,0)
debugline(&spaces,0)
;
}
;------------------------
dodisplaycache ()
{
JMP dodidi
MESSAGE tctmru = 'MRU = '
MESSAGE tctlru = 'LRU = '
MESSAGE title0 = 'CT     LRU    MRU    SEGM   '
MESSAGE title1 = 'FSEC   SECS   DRVE   HEAD   TRCK   LOCK'
LABEL dodidi

BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
numasc(BX,ct_mruD)
debugline(&tctmru,0)
debugline(&gnum,1)
;
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
numasc(BX,ct_lruD)
debugline(&tctlru,0)
debugline(&gnum,1)
debugline(&title0,0)
debugline(&title1,1)
;
DI = ct_mruD
REPEAT
   BX = &gnum
   BX.0 = 4
   PUSH DI
   numasc(BX,DI)
   debugline(&gnum,0)
   debugline(&spaces,0)
   POP DI
   BX = &gnum
   BX.0 = 4
   PUSH DI
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   DI = ES.DI.CTlruD.D
   numasc(BX,DI)
   debugline(&gnum,0)
   debugline(&spaces,0)
   POP DI
   BX = &gnum
   BX.0 = 4
   PUSH DI
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   DI = ES.DI.CTmruD.D
   numasc(BX,DI)
   debugline(&gnum,0)
   debugline(&spaces,0)
   POP DI
   BX = &gnum
   BX.0 = 4
   PUSH DI
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   DI = ES.DI.CTsegD.D
   numasc(BX,DI)
   debugline(&gnum,0)
   debugline(&spaces,0)
   POP DI
   BX = &gnum
   BX.0 = 4
   PUSH DI
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   AH = 0
   AL = ES.DI.CTfsector
   numasc(BX,AX)
   debugline(&gnum,0)
   debugline(&spaces,0)
   POP DI
   BX = &gnum
   BX.0 = 4
   PUSH DI
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   AL = ES.DI.CTsectors
   AH = 0
   numasc(BX,AX)
   debugline(&gnum,0)
   debugline(&spaces,0)
   POP DI
   BX = &gnum
   BX.0 = 4
   PUSH DI
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   AL = ES.DI.CTdrive
   AH = 0
   numasc(BX,AX)
   debugline(&gnum,0)
   debugline(&spaces,0)
   POP DI
   BX = &gnum
   BX.0 = 4
   PUSH DI
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   AL = ES.DI.CThead
   AH = 0
   numasc(BX,AX)
   debugline(&gnum,0)
   debugline(&spaces,0)
   POP DI
   BX = &gnum
   BX.0 = 4
   PUSH DI
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   AX = ES.DI.CTtrackD.D
   numasc(BX,AX)
   debugline(&gnum,0)
   debugline(&spaces,0)
   POP DI
   BX = &gnum
   BX.0 = 4
   PUSH DI
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   AL = ES.DI.CTlocked
   AH = 0
   numasc(BX,AX)
   debugline(&gnum,1)
   POP DI
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   DI = ES.DI.CTlruD.D
   EXIT (DI = 0FFFFH)
ENDREPL

}
;------------------------
displayinfo ()
{
SAVE AX,BX,CX,DX,DI,SI,ES
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
AL = int13_fsector
AH = 0
numasc(BX,AX)
debugline(&spaces,0)
debugline(&gnum,0)
;
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
AL = int13_sectors
AH = 0
numasc(BX,AX)
debugline(&spaces,0)
debugline(&gnum,0)
;
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
AL = int13_drive
AH = 0
numasc(BX,AX)
debugline(&spaces,0)
debugline(&gnum,0)
;
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
AL = int13_head
AH = 0
numasc(BX,AX)
debugline(&spaces,0)
debugline(&gnum,0)
;
BX = &gnum
BX.0 = 4
AX = int13_trackD
numasc(BX,AX)
debugline(&spaces,0)
debugline(&gnum,1)

}
;------------------------
numasc (nuascD,numbeD)
WORD
WORD
{
PUSH BX
PUSH CX
PUSH DX
PUSH DI
PUSH SI

DI = nuascD ;DI -> length of string
CH = 0
CL = DI.0 ;CX := length of string
;
;pre-fill the string with zeros
DI++
DO
  DI.0 = '0'
  DI++
  LOOP
END
;
DI = nuascD
CH = DI.0 ;CH := length of string
DI++
AX = numbeD
REPEAT
  BX = 16
  DX = 0
  DIV BX ;DX:AX/BX -> AX remainder DX
  IF (DL <= 9)
     DL += 48 ; convert to character
  ELSE
     DL -= 10
     DL += 'A'
  ENDIF
  DI.0 = DL
  INC CL ;keep count of accumulated ascii digits
  DEC CH
  EXIT (Z)
;  EXITuIF {AX = 0}
  INC DI
ENDREP
;
;we have the ascii representation left justified
;but with digits reversed - we must rectify the reversal.
;
SI = nuascD
SI.0 = CL ;so descriptor gets number length
INC CL
SHR CL,1 ;CL := INT((CL+1)/2)
CH = 0
SI += 1
DO
  AL = DI.0
  AH = SI.0
  SI.0 = AL
  DI.0 = AH
  INC SI
  DEC DI
  LOOP
END

POP SI
POP DI
POP DX
POP CX
POP BX
}
#ENDIF ;======
;-----------------------------------
pushall ()
{
axtempD = AX
POP AX ;AX := return address
retaddrD = AX
AX = axtempD
PUSH DS
PUSH ES
PUSH BP
PUSH DI
PUSH SI
PUSH DX
PUSH CX
PUSH BX
PUSH AX
JMP retaddrD
}
;-----------------------------
popall ()
{
POP AX
retaddrD = AX
POP AX
POP BX
POP CX
POP DX
POP SI
POP DI
POP BP
POP ES
POP DS
JMP retaddrD
}
;------------------------
promote_ct (ctD)
WORD
{
; promote the CT entry in ctD to the MRU
SAVE BX,DX,DI,SI,ES
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
DI = ct_mruD
BX = ctD
IF (DI <> BX)
   ; take BX out of list
   AX = ES.BX.CTlruD.D
   SI = ES.BX.CTmruD.D
   ES.SI.CTlruD.D = AX
   IF (AX = 0FFFFH)
      ct_lruD = SI
   ELSE
      PUSH BX
      BX = AX
      ES.BX.CTmruD.D = SI
      POP BX
   ENDIF
   ; put BX at MRU
   ES.DI.CTmruD.D = BX
   ES.BX.CTlruD.D = DI
   ES.BX.CTmruD.D = 0FFFFH
   ct_mruD = BX
ENDIF
}
;------------------------
demote_ct (ctD)
WORD
{
; demote the CT entry in ctD to the LRU
SAVE BX,DX,DI,SI,ES
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
DI = ct_lruD
BX = ctD
IF (DI <> BX)
   ; take BX out of list
   AX = ES.BX.CTmruD.D
   SI = ES.BX.CTlruD.D
   ES.SI.CTmruD.D = AX
   IF (AX = 0FFFFH)
      ct_mruD = SI
   ELSE
      PUSH BX
      BX = AX
      ES.BX.CTlruD.D = SI
      POP BX
   ENDIF
   ; put BX at LRU
   ES.DI.CTlruD.D = BX
   ES.BX.CTmruD.D = DI
   ES.BX.CTlruD.D = 0FFFFH
   ct_lruD = BX
ENDIF
}
;------------------------
scan_cache_for_sector ()
{
; scans the cache for the required sectors
; Returns: NC if not in cache
;          C if in cache, ES:AX = cache entry, DX = offset of sector (cache)

SAVE BX,CX,DI
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
DI = ct_mruD
XOR SI,SI
REPEAT
   DO
      EXITL (ES.DI.CTfsector = 0)
      AX = ES.DI.CTtrackD.D
      EXITL (AX <> int13_trackD)
      AL = ES.DI.CThead
      EXITL (AL <> int13_head)
      ;
      ; we already have part of this track cached!!
      ;
      ; Note: if we have read priority and the track was last written to,
      ;       then we must reread it all
      ;
      ; IF we are writing then there are two methods we can adopt:
      ;    1) Read in those sectors we dont know about (if any) and return
      ;       with the sectors in the cache
      ;    2) Demote this CT so that it gets used for writing the new sectors
      ; I think its best to do a mixture:
      ;    If and only if all the required sectors are in the cache
      ;    return with 'sectors in cache' else return with 'sectors NOT
      ;    in cache' but demote this CT so it gets reused
      ;
      ;
      ; IF we are reading then we can get the required extra sectors
      ;
      ; AL = CTfsector     : AH = AL + CTsectors - 1
      ; CL = newfs         : CH = CL + newns - 1
      ; Cases:
      ;    IF (CL >= AL && CH <= AH) ; have all required sectors: break
      ;    IF (CL > AH || CH < AL)   ; have none requested sectors
      ;       IF (CL > AH)
      ;          read from (AH + 1) for (CH - AH) sectors
      ;          set fsector to AL, sectors to CH - AL + 1
      ;       IF (CH < AL)
      ;          read from CL for (AL - CL) sectors
      ;          set fsector to CL, sectors to AH - CL + 1
      ;    IF (CL >= AL && CL <= AH) || (CH >= AL && CH <=AH) ; have some sectors
      ;       IF (CL < AL)
      ;          read from CL for (AL - CL) sectors
      ;          set fsector to CL, sectors to AH - CL + 1
      ;       IF (CH > AH)
      ;          read from (AH + 1) for (CH - AH) sectors
      ;          set fsector to AL, sectors to CH - AL + 1
      ;    IF (CL < AL && CH > AH) ; have some in middle
      ;        read from CL for (CH - CL + 1) sectors
      ;        set fsector to CL, set sectors to (CH - CL + 1)
      ;  We now have the sector:
      ;
      BL = ES.DI.CTfsector
      BH = BL + ES.DI.CTsectors
      BH--
      CL = newfs
      CH = CL + newns
      CH--
      ;
      IF (readpriority = 1 && int13_operation = 2) ; read
         ; check priorities
         IF (ES.DI.CTlastop = 3) ; write
            ; invalidate the CT
            clear_ct(DI)
            EXITL
         ENDIF
      ENDIF
      ;
      IF (int13_operation = 3) ; write
         IF (CL >= BL && CH <= BH)
            SI = 1
            EXITL
         ENDIF
         ; demote
         demote_ct(DI)
         EXITL
      ENDIF
      ;
      IF (CL >= BL && CH <= BH)
         ; have all sectors
         SI = 1
         EXITL
      ENDIF
      ;
      ; Clever little ditty to act intelligently to bring in sectors through
      ; a look ahead method
      ;  AICOUNT = 0 (initially)
      ;  DO
      ;    IF AICOUNT = 0 && newns = 1  AICOUNT = newfs EXIT
      ;    IF newfs = (AICOUNT+1) && newns = 1 AICOUNT = 0FFH EXIT
      ;    IF AICOUNT = 0FFH && sectors = 1  sectors = spt - newfs + 1 AItk = 0
      ;
      DO
         EXITL (restoftrack = 1 || readahead <> 0)
         IF (aicount = 0 && newns = 1)
            aicount = CL
            AX = ES.DI.CTtrackD.D
            DL = ES.DI.CTdrive
            DH = ES.DI.CThead
            aitrackD = AX
            aihead = DH
            aidrive = DL
            EXIT
         ENDIF
         EXIT (aicount = 0)
         DL = ES.DI.CTdrive
         DH = ES.DI.CThead
         AX = ES.DI.CTtrackD.D
         IF (AX <> aitrackD || DH <> aihead || DL <> aidrive)
            aicount = 0
            EXIT
         ENDIF
         AL = aicount
         AL++
         IF (AL = CL && newns = 1)
            CH = disk_spt
            #IF DEBUG
            PUSH AX
            debugline(&aiguess,0)
            POP AX
            #ENDIF
         ENDIF
         aicount = 0
      END
      ;
      ; check for read ahead
      IF (readahead <> 0 && restoftrack = 0)
         AL = CH + readahead
         IF (AL > disk_spt)
            AL = disk_spt
         ENDIF
         CH = AL
      ENDIF
      ;
      IFL (CL > BH || CH < BL)   ; have none requested sectors
         ; have none sectors
         IF (CL > BH)
            ; read from (BH + 1) for (CH - BH) sectors
            ; set fsector to BL, sectors to CH - BL + 1
            #IF DEBUG
            debugline(&readextra,0)
            #ENDIF
            DL = BL
            AL = CH - BL
            AL++
            DH = AL
            CH -= BH
            BH++
            readsectorsfromCT(DI,BH,CH)
            IF (NC)
               ES.DI.CTfsector = DL
               ES.DI.CTsectors = DH
            ENDIF
            SI++
            EXITL
         ENDIF
         IF (CH < BL)
            ; read from CL for (BL - CL) sectors
            ; set fsector to CL, sectors to BH - CL + 1
            #IF DEBUG
            debugline(&readextra,0)
            #ENDIF
            DL = CL
            AL = BH - CL
            AL++
            DH = AL
            BL -= CL
            readsectorsfromCT(DI,CL,BL)
            IF (NC)
               ES.DI.CTfsector = DL
               ES.DI.CTsectors = DH
            ENDIF
            SI++
            EXITL
         ENDIF
      ENDIF
      ;
      IFL ((CL >= BL && CL <= BH) || (CH >= BL && CH <=BH)) ; have some sectors
         IF (CL < BL)
            ; read from CL for (BL - CL) sectors
            ; set fsector to CL, sectors to BH - CL + 1
            #IF DEBUG
            debugline(&readextra,0)
            #ENDIF
            DL = CL
            AL = BH - CL
            AL++
            DH = AL
            BL -= CL
            readsectorsfromCT(DI,CL,BL)
            IF (NC)
               ES.DI.CTfsector = DL
               ES.DI.CTsectors = DH
            ENDIF
            SI++
            EXIT
         ENDIF
         IF (CH > BH)
            ; read from (BH + 1) for (CH - BH) sectors
            ; set fsector to BL, sectors to CH - BL + 1
            #IF DEBUG
            debugline(&readextra,0)
            #ENDIF
            DL = BL
            AL = CH - BL
            AL++
            DH = AL
            CH -= BH
            BH++
            readsectorsfromCT(DI,BH,CH)
            IF (NC)
               ES.DI.CTfsector = DL
               ES.DI.CTsectors = DH
            ENDIF
            SI++
            EXIT
         ENDIF
      ENDIF
      IF (CL < BL && CH > BH)
         ; we have the sectors in between what we want, must reread the track
         ; read from CL for (CH-CL+1) sectors
         ; set fsector to CL, sectors to (CH-CL+1)
         #IF DEBUG
         debugline(&readextra,0)
         #ENDIF
         DL = CL
         DH = CH - CL
         DH++
         readsectorsfromCT(DI,DL,DH)
         IF (NC)
            ES.DI.CTfsector = DL
            ES.DI.CTsectors = DH
         ENDIF
         SI++
         EXIT
      ENDIF
    END
    EXIT (SI = 1)
    aicount = 0
    DI = ES.DI.CTlruD.D
    EXIT (DI = 0FFFFH)
ENDREPL
IF (SI = 1 && errorcode = 0)
   AL = newfs
   AL--
   AH = 0
   CX = disk_bpsD
   MUL CX
   DX = AX ; offset in CT segment of first sector
   AX = DI ; address of CT entry
   STC
ELSE
   CLC
ENDIF
}
;------------------------
readsectorsfromCT (ctoffD,ctfirst,ctnumber)
WORD
BYTE
BYTE
{
; read sectors starting at ctfirst for ctnumber according
; to information in CT ctoffD
SAVE BX,CX,DX,SI,DI,ES
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
DI = ctoffD

DL = ES.DI.CTdrive
DH = ES.DI.CThead

AL = ctfirst
AH = 0
AL--
CX = disk_bpsD
PUSH DX
MUL CX
POP DX
SI = AX
BX = ES.DI.CTsegD.D

CX = ES.DI.CTtrackD.D

AL = memorytype
IF (AL = EXTENDED || AL = EXPANDED)
   PUSH BX
   BX = tracksegD
ENDIF

int13read(BX,SI,DL,DH,CX,ctfirst,ctnumber)
; if fail CY
errorcode = AH

DO
   EXIT (memorytype = CONVENTIONAL)
   POP ES
   EXIT (errorcode <> 0)
   ; copy from the temp track into the cache
   DI = SI
   AL = ctnumber
   AH = 0
   CX = disk_bpsD
   MUL CX
   CX = AX

   conv_to_cache(tracksegD,SI,CX,ES)

   AH = errorcode
END
IF (errorcode = 0)
   CLC
ELSE
   STC
ENDIF
}
;------------------------
read_from_cache (readctD,readsectorD)
WORD
WORD
{
; transfer from the cache into memory
; sector at readsectorD in CT readCTD

SAVE CX,DX,DI,SI

; sector is in cache: readctD (CT), DX (sector offset in cache)
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
BX = readctD
DX = ES.BX.CTsegD.D
promote_ct(BX)
DI = int13_buffer.0.D
AX = int13_buffer.2.D
ES = AX
SI = readsectorD
AX = disk_bpsD
CL = newns
CH = 0
PUSH DX
MUL CX
POP DX
CX = AX

cache_to_conv (ES,DI,CX,DX,SI)

}
;------------------------
cache_to_conv (csegD,coffD,cbytesD,ctsegD,ctoffD)
WORD
WORD
WORD
WORD
WORD
{
SAVE BX,CX,DX,SI,DI,ES

; copy the contents of the cache from offset ctoffD within the CT
; to conventional memory at csegD:coffD for cbytesD bytes

AL = memorytype
DO
   IF (AL = CONVENTIONAL)
      PUSH DS
      SI = ctoffD
      DI = coffD
      AX = csegD
      ES = AX
      CX = cbytesD
      SHR CX,1
      AX = ctsegD
      IF (is386 = 0)
         DS = AX
         MOVS WIR
      ELSE
         SHR CX,1
         DS = AX
         #.386
         MOVS DIR
         #.8086
      ENDIF
      POP DS
      EXITL
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = EXTENDED)
      SI = &xmsblock
      AX = cbytesD
      SI.XMlen.0.D = AX
      XOR AX,AX
      SI.XMlen.2.D = AX
      SI.XMhdestD.D = AX
      AX = coffD
      SI.XMdest.0.D = AX
      AX = csegD
      SI.XMdest.2.D = AX
      AX = xmmhandleD
      SI.XMhsourceD.D = AX
      AX = ctsegD
      CX = 512
      MUL CX
      AX += ctoffD
      IF (C)
         DX++
      ENDIF
      SI.XMsource.0.D = AX
      SI.XMsource.2.D = DX
      AH = 0BH
      CALL DWORD PTR xms
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = EXPANDED)
      ; map expanded pages into EMM seg
      ; find which LP the CT starts in
      AX = ctsegD ; 512 byte page
      CX = 512
      MUL CX
      CX = 16384 ; 16K
      DIV CX
      ; LPn is in AX, offset in DX
      ; map LPn,n+1 into PP0,1 as the CT will not be bigger than 32K
      PUSH DX ; save offset
      DX = emmhandleD
      BX = AX
      PUSH BX
      AX = 4400H
      INT 67H
      POP BX
      BX++
      AX = 4401H
      INT 67H
      ; CT is now in emmsegD:offset
      POP AX ; offset
      CX = 16
      XOR DX,DX
      DIV CX
      AX += emmsegD
      ; segment is in AX
      DX = AX
      ; start of CT is at ES:0
      SI = ctoffD
      DI = coffD
      AX = csegD
      ES = AX
      PUSH DS
      CX = cbytesD
      SHR CX,1
      IF (is386 = 0)
         DS = DX
         MOVS WIR
      ELSE
         SHR CX,1
         DS = DX
         #.386
         MOVS DIR
         #.8086
      ENDIF
      POP DS
      EXIT
   ENDIF
END

}
;------------------------
read_into_cache ()
{

SAVE BX,CX

; read the requested sectors into the cache
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
DI = ct_lruD
REPEAT
   EXIT (ES.DI.CTlocked = 0)
   DI = ES.DI.CTmruD.D
   EXIT (DI = 0FFFFH)
ENDREP
IF (DI = 0FFFFH)
   ; all CTs are locked
   ; so read from disk to memory
   CL = newfs
   CH = newns
   DL = int13_drive
   DH = int13_head
   BX = int13_buffer.0.D
   AX = int13_buffer.2.D
   ES = AX
   int13read(ES,BX,DL,DH,int13_trackD,CL,CH)
   errorcode = AH
   ;
   AX = 0FFFFH
   CLC
   RETURN
ENDIF

CL = newfs
CH = 0
CL--
AX = disk_bpsD
MUL CX
BX = AX
CL++

DH = int13_head
DL = int13_drive
AX = ES.DI.CTsegD.D
ES = AX

CH = newns
IF (restoftrack = 1)
   AL = disk_spt
   CH = AL - CL + 1
ELSE
   IF (readahead <> 0)
      AL = CL + CH - 1
      IF (AL < disk_spt)
         AL += readahead
         IF (AL > disk_spt)
            AL = disk_spt
         ENDIF
         AL -= CL
         AL++
         CH = AL
      ENDIF
   ENDIF
ENDIF

; use the temporary track
AL = memorytype
IF (AL = EXTENDED || AL = EXPANDED)
   PUSH ES
   AX = tracksegD
   ES = AX
ENDIF

int13read(ES,BX,DL,DH,int13_trackD,CL,CH)
; returns AX and Cflag with codes
errorcode = AH

DO
   EXIT (memorytype = CONVENTIONAL)
   POP ES
   EXIT (errorcode <> 0)
   ; copy temp track into cache
   PUSH CX
   PUSH DX
   PUSH DI
   SI = BX
   DI = BX
   AL = CH
   AH = 0
   CX = disk_bpsD
   MUL CX
   CX = AX

   conv_to_cache (tracksegD,SI,CX,ES)

   POP DI
   POP DX
   POP CX
END

IFL (errorcode = 0)
   PUSH BX
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   ES.DI.CTfsector = CL
   ES.DI.CTsectors = CH
   BX = int13_trackD
   ES.DI.CTtrackD.D = BX
   DH = int13_head
   ES.DI.CThead = DH
   DL = int13_drive
   ES.DI.CTdrive = DL
   ES.DI.CTlastop = 2 ; read
   ;
   ; special code to deal with the floppy disks
   ; if this is the first read of the boot sector, then we must
   ; extract bps and spt
   IFL (CL = 1 && BX = 0 && DH = 0 && (DL = 0 || DL = 1))
      ; boot sector of a floppy drive
      #IF DEBUG
      debugline(&floppy,0)
      #ENDIF
      PUSH ES
      PUSH DX
      SI = &drivetable
      AL = DL
      AH = 0
      CX = DRIVEDEF
      MUL CX
      SI += AX
      AL = memorytype
      IF (AL = CONVENTIONAL)
         ; look at CTsegD:0B for bps
         AX = ES.DI.CTsegD.D
         ES = AX
      ELSE
         AX = tracksegD
         ES = AX
      ENDIF
      AX = ES.0BH.D ; bps
      CX = ES.18H.D ; spt
      POP DX
      POP ES
      ; only trust a sensible BPB (a zero spt would divide by zero, and a
      ; track bigger than a CT would overrun it); otherwise the geometry
      ; stays unknown and the drive is passed straight to the BIOS
      IF (AX = max_bpsD && CL <> 0 && CX <= max_sptD)
         ES.DI.CTlocked = 1
         SI.DRVbpsD.D = AX
         disk_bpsD = AX
         SI.DRVspt = CL
         disk_spt = CL
         IF (DL = 0)
            floppy0ok = 1
         ELSE
            floppy1ok = 1
         ENDIF
      ELSE
         ; we cant tell what we have read, so dont keep it
         ES.DI.CTfsector = 0
      ENDIF
   ENDIF
   POP BX
   promote_ct(DI)
   CLC
ELSE
   ; invalidate the CT, as the failed read may have overwritten its data
   ; (ES is the CT data here, not the descriptors)
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   ES.DI.CTfsector = 0
   STC
ENDIF

AX = DI ; CT entry
DX = BX ; offset of first sector
}
;------------------------
conv_to_cache (csegD,coffD,cbytesD,ctsegD)
WORD
WORD
WORD
WORD
{
SAVE BX,CX,DX,DI,SI,ES

; copy data from conventional memory (csegD:coffD) into the
; cache at offset csegD within the CT, for cbytesD bytes.

AL = memorytype
DO
   IF (AL = CONVENTIONAL)
      PUSH DS
      SI = coffD
      DI = SI
      AX = ctsegD
      ES = AX
      CX = cbytesD
      SHR CX,1
      AX = csegD
      IF (is386 = 0)
         DS = AX
         MOVS WIR
      ELSE
         SHR CX,1
         DS = AX
         #.386
         MOVS DIR
         #.8086
      ENDIF
      POP DS
      EXITL
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = EXTENDED)
      SI = &xmsblock
      AX = cbytesD
      SI.XMlen.0.D = AX
      XOR AX,AX
      SI.XMlen.2.D = AX
      SI.XMhsourceD.D = AX
      AX = coffD
      SI.XMsource.0.D = AX
      AX = csegD
      SI.XMsource.2.D = AX
      AX = xmmhandleD
      SI.XMhdestD.D = AX
      AX = ctsegD
      CX = 512
      MUL CX
      AX += coffD
      IF (C)
         DX++
      ENDIF
      SI.XMdest.0.D = AX
      SI.XMdest.2.D = DX
      AH = 0BH
      CALL DWORD PTR xms
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = EXPANDED)
      ; map required page into emmsegD
      ; find which LP the CT starts in
      AX = ctsegD ; 512 byte page
      CX = 512
      MUL CX
      CX = 16384 ; 16K
      DIV CX
      ; LPn is in AX, offset in DX
      ; map LPn,n+1 into PP0,1 as the CT will not be bigger than 32K
      PUSH DX ; save offset
      DX = emmhandleD
      BX = AX
      PUSH BX
      AX = 4400H
      INT 67H
      POP BX
      BX++
      AX = 4401H
      INT 67H
      ; CT is now in emmsegD:offset
      POP AX ; offset
      CX = 16
      XOR DX,DX
      DIV CX
      AX += emmsegD
      ; segment is in AX
      ES = AX
      ; start of CT is at ES:0
      DI = coffD
      SI = DI
      PUSH DS
      CX = cbytesD
      SHR CX,1
      AX = csegD
      IF (is386 = 0)
         DS = AX
         MOVS WIR
      ELSE
         SHR CX,1
         DS = AX
         #.386
         MOVS DIR
         #.8086
      ENDIF
      POP DS
      EXIT
   ENDIF
END
}
;------------------------
int13read (i13segD,i13offD,i13drive,i13head,i13trackD,i13fsec,i13secs)
WORD
WORD
BYTE
BYTE
WORD
BYTE
BYTE
{
SAVE BX,CX,DX,SI,DI,ES

; read from the disk via old INT13
DI = 2
REPEAT
   PUSH DI
   CL = i13fsec
   AX = i13trackD
   CH = AL
   SHR AX,1
   SHR AX,1
   AND AL,11000000B
   OR CL,AL
   DH = i13head
   DL = i13drive
   AX = i13segD
   ES = AX
   BX = i13offD
   AL = i13secs

   AH = 2
   CLI
   PUSHF
   CALL DWORD PTR normINT13
   POP DI
   EXIT (NC)
   ;
   DI--
   IF (DI = 0)
      STC
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   AH = 0
   DL = drive
   IF (DL = 0FFH)
      DL = 80H
   ENDIF
   CLI
   PUSHF
   CALL DWORD PTR normINT13
ENDREP

PUSHF
PUSH AX
physicals.0.D += 1
IF (C)
   physicals.2.D += 1
ENDIF
POP AX
POPF

}
;------------------------
int13write (i13segD,i13offD,i13drive,i13head,i13trackD,i13fsec,i13secs)
WORD
WORD
BYTE
BYTE
WORD
BYTE
BYTE
{
SAVE BX,CX,DX,SI,DI,ES

; write to the disk via old INT13
DI = 2
REPEAT
   PUSH DI
   CL = i13fsec
   AX = i13trackD
   CH = AL
   SHR AX,1
   SHR AX,1
   AND AL,11000000B
   OR CL,AL
   DH = i13head
   DL = i13drive
   AX = i13segD
   ES = AX
   BX = i13offD
   AL = i13secs

   AH = 3
   CLI
   PUSHF
   CALL DWORD PTR normINT13
   POP DI
   EXIT (NC)
   ;
   DI--
   IF (DI = 0)
      STC
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   AH = 0
   DL = drive
   IF (DL = 0FFH)
      DL = 80H
   ENDIF
   CLI
   PUSHF
   CALL DWORD PTR normINT13
ENDREP

PUSHF
PUSH AX
physicals.0.D += 1
IF (C)
   physicals.2.D += 1
ENDIF
POP AX
POPF

}
;------------------------
write_to_cache (writectD)
WORD
WORD
{

; Transfer from memory to the cache and promote,

SAVE BX,CX

; copy the requested sectors into the cache from memory
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
SI = writectD
promote_ct(SI)

ES.SI.CTlastop = 3 ; write
AL = int13_drive
ES.SI.CTdrive = AL
AL = int13_head
ES.SI.CThead = AL
AX = int13_trackD
ES.SI.CTtrackD.D = AX
BL = newns
ES.SI.CTsectors = BL
AL = newfs
ES.SI.CTfsector = AL

AL--
AH = 0
CX = disk_bpsD
MUL CX
DI = AX

AL = BL
AH = 0
MUL CX
CX = AX

; copy the sectors from memory into the cache
PUSH SI ; save CT entry
PUSH ES

AX = ES.SI.CTsegD.D ; dest seg
ES = AX

AL = memorytype
IF (AL = EXTENDED || AL = EXPANDED)
   ; use temp track
   PUSH ES
   AX = tracksegD
   ES = AX
ENDIF

; copy to conv memory or to temp track
PUSH CX
PUSH DI
PUSH DS
SI = int13_buffer.0.D
AX = int13_buffer.2.D
SHR CX,1
IF (is386 = 0)
   DS = AX
   MOVS WIR
ELSE
   SHR CX,1
   DS = AX
   #.386
   MOVS DIR
   #.8086
ENDIF
POP DS
POP DI
POP CX

AL = memorytype
IF (AL = EXTENDED || AL = EXPANDED)
   ; copy temp track to cache
   POP ES
   conv_to_cache(tracksegD,DI,CX,ES)
ENDIF

POP ES
POP SI ; restore ES entry

}
;------------------------
write_to_disk ()
{
; write the INT13 call to disk

SAVE BX,CX,DX,SI

BX = int13_buffer.0.D
AX = int13_buffer.2.D
ES = AX
SI = int13_trackD
DL = int13_drive
DH = int13_head
CL = newfs
CH = newns

int13write(ES,BX,DL,DH,SI,CL,CH)
; returns C if error
errorcode = AH

}
;------------------------
compare_cache (cctD)
WORD
WORD
{
; compare the cache sectors at CT cctD, offset csectorD
; with whats in memory at int13_buffer

SAVE BX,CX,DX

AX = cachesegD
ES = AX

IF (allowredundant = 1)
   CLC
   RETURN
ENDIF

BX = cctD
DX = ES.BX.CTsegD.D

PUSH DX
AL = newfs
AH = 0
AL--
CX = disk_bpsD
MUL CX
SI = AX

AL = newns
AH = 0
MUL CX
CX = AX
POP DX

DI = int13_buffer.0.D
AX = int13_buffer.2.D
ES = AX

AL = memorytype
IF (AL = EXTENDED || AL = EXPANDED)
   ; copy from cache to temp track first
   cache_to_conv(tracksegD,SI,CX,DX,SI)
   DX = tracksegD
ENDIF

PUSH DS
DS = DX
CLD
REPZ CMPSB
POP DS
; test Z, not CX = 0: CX also reaches 0 when only the last byte differs
IF (Z)
   ; equal
   STC
ELSE
   ; not equal
   CLC
ENDIF
}
;------------------------
flush_cache (fdrive)
BYTE
{
; clear the cache of drive fdrive (if fdrive = 0FFH - all drives)
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
DI = ct_lruD
REPEAT
   AL = ES.DI.CTdrive
   IF (AL = fdrive || fdrive = 0FFH)
      clear_ct (DI)
   ENDIF
   DI = ES.DI.CTmruD.D
   EXIT (DI = 0FFFFH)
ENDREP

; clear vaiables
XOR AX,AX
aicount = AL
logicals.0.D = AX
logicals.2.D = AX
physicals.0.D = AX
physicals.2.D = AX
IF (fdrive = 0 || fdrive = 0FFH)
   floppy0ok = AL
ENDIF
IF (fdrive = 1 || fdrive = 0FFH)
   floppy1ok = AL
ENDIF

}
;------------------------
clear_ct (cctD)
WORD
{
; clear a CT entry
PUSH DI
DI = cctD
XOR AX,AX
ES.DI.CTtrackD.D = AX
ES.DI.CTdrive = AL
ES.DI.CThead = AL
ES.DI.CTfsector = AL
ES.DI.CTsectors = AL
ES.DI.CTlocked = AL
ES.DI.CTlastop = AL
POP DI
}
;------------------------
testdrive(drv)
BYTE
{
; test to see if the drive is enabled in the drivetable
PUSH BX
PUSH CX
PUSH DX
BX = &drivetable
AL = drv
IF (AL >= 80H)
   AL -= 80H
   AL += 2
ENDIF
CL = DRIVEDEF
MUL CL
BX += AX
IF (BX.DRVid = drv && BX.DRVtype <> 0)
   AL = drv
   IF (AL = 0 && floppy0ok = 0)
      BX.DRVspt = 8
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 1 && floppy1ok = 0)
      BX.DRVspt = 8
   ENDIF
   AL = BX.DRVspt
   disk_spt = AL
   AX = BX.DRVbpsD.D
   disk_bpsD = AX
   AL = BX.DRVheads
   disk_heads = AL
   STC
ELSE
   #IF DEBUG
   debugline(&wrongdrive,1)
   #ENDIF
   CLC
ENDIF
POP DX
POP CX
POP BX
}
;------------------------
geometryknown (gkdrive)
BYTE
{
; returns C if we know the spt of drive gkdrive (from the boot sector,
; if it is a floppy), else NC
AL = 1
IF (gkdrive = 0)
   AL = floppy0ok
ENDIF
IF (gkdrive = 1)
   AL = floppy1ok
ENDIF
IF (AL = 0)
   CLC
ELSE
   STC
ENDIF
}
;------------------------
check_for_more ()
{
; checks to see if there are more tracks to read
; and sets up the varaibles
; Returns C if more

PUSH BX
PUSH CX
PUSH DX

IF (int13_sectors = 0 || moretodo = 0)
   CLC
ELSE
   ; update the address
   BX = int13_buffer.0.D
   AL = newns
   AH = 0
   CX = disk_bpsD
   MUL CX
   BX += AX
   IF (C)
      int13_buffer.2.D += 1000H
   ENDIF
   int13_buffer.0.D = BX
   ;
   moretodo--
   newfs = 1
   DH = int13_head
   DH++
   IF (DH = disk_heads)
      int13_trackD++
      DH = 0
   ENDIF
   int13_head = DH
   CL = int13_sectors
   IF (CL > disk_spt)
      CL -= disk_spt
      newns = disk_spt
   ELSE
      newns = CL
      CL = 0
   ENDIF
   int13_sectors = CL
   STC
ENDIF
POP DX
POP CX
POP BX
}
;------------------------
uninstall_tsr ()
{

; uninstall ourselves from memory

DO
   ; see if the INT13 vector is ours
   AX = 3513H
   INT 21H
   AX = ES
   CX = CS
   IF (AX <> CX)
      CLC
      EXITL
   ENDIF
   ;
   ; restore INT 13
   PUSH DS
   DX = normINT13.0.D
   AX = normINT13.2.D
   DS = AX
   AX = 2513H
   INT 21H
   POP DS
   ;
   ; free conventional memory
   AX = pspD
   ES = AX
   AH = 49H
   INT 21H
   ;
   ; free CTs if not CONVENTIONAL
   AX = cachesegD
   ES = AX
   XOR DI,DI
   CX = number_ctsD
   AL = memorytype
   DO
      EXIT (AL = CONVENTIONAL)
      IF (AL = EXTENDED)
         BX = xmmhandleD
         IF (BX <> 0)
            dealoc_extended(BX)
         ENDIF
         EXIT
      ENDIF
      IF (AL = EXPANDED)
         BX = emmhandleD
         IF (BX <> 0)
            dealoc_expanded(BX)
         ENDIF
      ENDIF
   END
   ;
   ; free any UMBs we might have used
   DO
      EXIT (umbs = 0 || umbs = 0FFH)
      AL = umbs
      TEST AL,1
      IF (NZ)
         ; free the CT
         PUSH AX
         dealoc_umb(cachesegD)
         POP AX
      ENDIF
      TEST AL,2
      IF (NZ)
         ; free the temp track
         BX = tracksegD
         IF (BX <> 0)
            dealoc_umb(BX)
         ENDIF
      ENDIF
   END
   ;
   STC
END
}
;------------------------
dealoc_extended (xhandleD)
WORD
{
; deallocate the XMB
DX = xhandleD
AH = 0AH
CALL DWORD PTR xms
}
;------------------------
dealoc_expanded(phandleD)
WORD
{
; dealocate the EMB
DX = phandleD
AH = 45H
INT 67H
}
;------------------------
dealoc_umb (uhandleD)
WORD
{
; deallocate the UMB
AX = uhandleD
ES = AX
AH = 49H
INT 21H
}
;------------------------
savestate()
{
SAVE AX,BX,DX,ES
AL = memorytype
DO
   EXIT (AL = CONVENTIONAL)
   IF (AL = EXTENDED)
      ; get state of A20 line
      AH = 7
      CALL DWORD PTR xms
      a20state = AL
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = EXPANDED)
      ; save page map
      AH = 47H
      DX = emmhandleD
      INT 67H
      EXIT
   ENDIF
END
}
;------------------------
restorestate()
{
SAVE AX,BX,DX,ES
AL = memorytype
DO
   EXIT (AL = CONVENTIONAL)
   IF (AL = EXTENDED)
      ; restore A20 line
      AH = 5 ; enable
      IF (a20state = 0)
         AH++ ; disable
      ENDIF
      CALL DWORD PTR xms
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = EXPANDED)
      ; restore page map
      AH = 48H
      DX = emmhandleD
      INT 67H
      EXIT
   ENDIF
END
}
;------------------------
waitfffb ()
{
PUSH AX
PUSH DX
DX = 03DAH
;wait for ffb
DO
   IN AL,DX
   AND AL,00001000B
   CONTINUE (Z)
END
POP DX
POP AX
}
;-----------------------------
invertvideo ()
{
AH = AL
IF (displayparaD = 0B000H)
   AND AH,01110000B
   AND AL,00000111B
   IF (AH = 70H && AL = 0)
      AL = 00001111B
   ELSE
      AL = 01110000B
   ENDIF
ELSE
   CL = 4
   SHL AH,CL
   SHR AL,CL
   OR AL,AH
   AND AL,07FH
ENDIF
}
;-----------------------------
sethit()
{
PUSH AX
PUSH CX
PUSH ES
waitfffb()
AX = displayparaD
ES = AX
AX = ES.158.D
oldhitD = AX
AL = AH
invertvideo()
AH = AL
AL = 'H'
ES.158.D = AX
POP ES
POP CX
POP AX
}
;------------------------
clearhit()
{
PUSH AX
PUSH ES
waitfffb()
AX = displayparaD
ES = AX
AX = oldhitD
ES.158.D = AX
POP ES
POP AX
}
;------------------------
; END OF RESIDENT CODE
;------------------------
init_data ()
{
; this 16K chunk will allow room for 1024 descriptors
; which can contain 8Mb of cache
LIST bootsector (16384)	; space for reading in sector of HD
	; also for allowing gap for CT descriptors
	; so we dont overwrite our code!
LIST initstack (280)

#IF DVERSION
MESSAGE start0d = 'MI Systems  MI-CACHE Disk Cache Utility  Version 1.0 (DEBUG)'
#ELSE
MESSAGE start0 = 'MI Systems  MI-CACHE Disk Cache Utility  Version 1.0'
#ENDIF
MESSAGE start1 = 'Copyright (C) 1992. All rights reserved.'
MESSAGE nodrive = 'Must specify drive'
MESSAGE errordrive = 'Error in determining drive'
MESSAGE invalidparam = 'Invalid parameter'
MESSAGE baddos = 'Must have DOS version 2.10 or greater'
MESSAGE baddosumb = 'Must have DOS version 5.0 to use UMBs'
MESSAGE insufmem = 'Insufficient memory to create cache'
MESSAGE instld = 'MI-CACHE is now loaded'
MESSAGE uninstalled = 'MI-CACHE has been unloaded from memory'
MESSAGE cannotunin = 'Unable to unload MI-CACHE'
MESSAGE notinstalled = 'MI-CACHE is not loaded'
MESSAGE alreadyin = 'MI-CACHE is already loaded'
MESSAGE reqtoosmall = 'Cache must be at least 64K - adjusting size'

MESSAGE xmmnotexist = 'Extended Memory Manager is not loaded'
MESSAGE emmnotexist = 'Expanded Memory Manager is not loaded'
MESSAGE emmwrong = 'Require EMM Version 3.2 or greater'
MESSAGE umbnotexist = 'Upper Memory Blocks are not available'
MESSAGE errorincmemaloc = 'Memory allocation error'
MESSAGE errorinxmemaloc = 'Error whilst allocating extended memory'
MESSAGE errorinememaloc = 'Error whilst allocating expanded memory'

MESSAGE cachedisabled = 'MI-CACHE has been disabled'
MESSAGE cacheenabled = 'MI-CACHE has been enabled'
MESSAGE butdisabled = ', but disabled'
MESSAGE flushed = 'Cache has been flushed'

MESSAGE cacheisin = 'Cache is in '
MESSAGE ext_t = 'extended memory'
MESSAGE exp_t = 'expanded memory'
MESSAGE con_t = 'conventional memory'
MESSAGE codeused = 'Conventional memory used = '
MESSAGE mcacheused = 'Size of cache            = '
MESSAGE ink = ' Kbytes'

LIST emmname = 'EMMXXXX0',0

WORD strategyD
BYTE linkflag

LIST hugetable (12)

LIST dnumber (12)
}
;------------------------
init ()
{
AX = ES
pspD = AX
AX = DS
datasegD = AX

#IF DVERSION
displayline(&start0d,1)
#ELSE
displayline(&start0,1)
#ENDIF
displayline(&start1,1)
displayNL()

; free the envirnment block
AX = ES.2CH.D
ES = AX
AH = 49H
INT 21H

; get the DOS version
AX = 3000H
INT 21H
XCHG AL,AH
IF (AX < 020AH)
   displayline(&baddos,1)
   CLC
   RETURN
ENDIF
dosversionD = AX

; we need to know if we are already installed
; see if we are installed
installed = 0
AX = 0FF00H
CL = 'M'
CH = 'I'
INT 13H
IF (CL = 'O' && CH = 'k')
   installed = 1
ENDIF

; parse the command line
requestedKD = 0
memorytype = MEMUNDEFINED
dosdrive = 0FFH
readahead = 0
restoftrack = 1
aicount = 0
allowredundant = 0
minimise = 0
AX = pspD
ES = AX
SI = 80H
CL = ES.SI.0
CH = 0
SI++
DO
   EXITL (CL = 0)
   AL = ES.SI.0
   SI++
   EXITL (AL = 13)
   CONTINUE (AL = 32)
   uppercase()
   IF (AL >= 'A' && AL <= 'Z')
      ; assume a drive
      AH = ES.SI.0
      SI++
      EXITL (AH = 13)
      IF (AH = ':')
         dosdrive = AL - 'A'
         CONTINUE
      ENDIF
      ; invalid parameter
   ENDIF
   IF (AL >= '0' && AL <= '9')
      ; assume memory size
      SI--
      cl_asc2num()
      ; DX has requested K, AL has last char
      PUSH AX
      BX = DX
      requestedKD = BX
      IF (BX < 64)
         displayline(&reqtoosmall,1)
         requestedKD = 64
      ENDIF
      POP AX
      EXIT (AL = 13)
      CONTINUEL
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = '-' || AL = '/')
      ; parameters
      AL = ES.SI.0
      SI++
      EXIT (AL = 13)
      uppercase()
      parseparameter(AL)
      CONTINUEL (C) ; ok
      ; invalid parameter
   ENDIF
   ; invalid
   displayline(&invalidparam,1)
   CLC
   RETURN
END

; If dosdrive = 0FFH - cache any drive  Set drive = 0FFH
; If dosdrive <> 0FFH - cache this drive only Set drive to dosdrive
IFL (uninstall = 1)
   IF (installed = 0)
      displayline(&notinstalled,1)
      AX = 4C01H
      INT 21H
   ENDIF
   ; ask MICACHE to free all of its memory and restore the vectors
   AX = 0FF01H
   CL = 'M'
   CH = 'I'
   INT 13H
   IF (AL = 'O' && AH = 'k')
      ; successful
      displayline(&uninstalled,1)
      AL = 0
   ELSE
      ; cannot uninstall
      displayline(&cannotunin,1)
      AL = 1
   ENDIF
   AH = 4CH
   INT 21H
ENDIF
IF (displaycache = 1)
   AX = 0FF02H
   CL = 'M'
   CH = 'I'
   INT 13H
   AX = 4C00H
   INT 21H
ENDIF

AL = dosdrive
IF (AL = 0FFH && installed = 0)
   displayline(&nodrive,1)
   AX = 4C01H
   INT 21H
ENDIF
IF (AL >= 2)
   AL -= 2
   OR AL,80H
ENDIF
drive = AL

IFL (installed = 1)
   ; use only installed features
   DO
      IF (disable = 1)
         ; disable the cache
         AX = 0FF03H
         DL = 0
         CL = 'M'
         CH = 'I'
         INT 13H
         ; assume ok
         displayline(&cachedisabled,1)
         EXITL
      ENDIF
      IF (disable = 2)
         ; enable the cache
         AX = 0FF03H
         CL = 'M'
         CH = 'I'
         DL = 1
         INT 13H
         ; assume ok
         displayline(&cacheenabled,1)
         EXITL
      ENDIF
      IF (rflush = 1)
         ; flush the cache
         AX = 0FF04H
         CL = 'M'
         CH = 'I'
         INT 13H
         ; assume ok
         displayline(&flushed,1)
         EXIT
      ENDIF
      IF (showmeasures = 1)
         ; get cache measurements
         AX = 0FF05H
         CL = 'M'
         CH = 'I'
         INT 13H
         ; assume ok, ES:BX points to measurement data
         ; DX has size of cache (K), AL has memory type
         show_measurements(DX,ES,BX,AL)
         EXIT
      ENDIF
      IF (showparas = 1)
         ; get cache parameters
         AX = 0FF06H
         CL = 'M'
         CH = 'I'
         INT 13H
         ; assume ok, ES:BX points to parameter table, AL mem
         show_parameters(ES,BX,AL)
         EXIT
      ENDIF
      installedhelp()
   END
   AX = 4C00H
   INT 21H
ENDIF

; check we have DOS 5.0 for UMBs
umbs = 0FFH
IF (dosversionD < 0500H)
   umbs = 0
ENDIF
; check if the UMBs exist by trying to allocate one
;
; allocate UMB block and return segment in AX and C
; else NC and if no umbs AX =0FFFFH, or AX = avail paras
aloc_umb(24576) ; in paras (384K)
IF (AX = 0FFFFH)
   umbs = 0
ENDIF
;
; umbs = 0    - no UMBs
;      = 0FFH - have UMBs but we dont use any
;      = 1    - use UMB for CT descriptors
;      = 2    - use UMB for temp track
;      = 3    - use UMBs for both

check_memory()
IF (NC)
   AX = 4C02H
   INT 21H
ENDIF

; we want requestedparsD after the end of our code
;AX = &endofcode
AX = &init_data
AX += 15
CX = 16
XOR DX,DX
DIV CX
CX = CS
AX += CX
AX += 2
; ax has segment address of free memory, ie. cache descriptors + cache
cachesegD = AX

getdisplaytype()
build_drive_table()
IF (NC)
   displayline(&errordrive,1)
   AX = 4C01H
   INT 21H
ENDIF

; NOTE: the above method must take into accout for differert formats of
; drive, ie: 3inch floppy can be 9 or 18 sectors, but this will only
; report 19 as the maximum, and Hard disk of 17 sectors!!
; In our AI methods we need to know the exact number of spt of the disk!
;
; To do this: use INT13 (08H) to get the number of floppy drives in DL, and
; INT13 (15H) with DL = 80H,81H.. to get the type of each hard disk (AL) - if
; AL <> 3 then no more hard disks
  
; calculate the size of one CT
AX = max_bpsD
CX = max_sptD
MUL CX
ct_lengthD = AX
CX = 16
DIV CX
ct_lengthinparasD = AX

; calculate how many CTs we can have
AX = requestedKD
CX = 1024
MUL CX
; in bytes
CX = ct_lengthD
DIV CX
; in AX
number_ctsD = AX

; first we should try and allocate UMBs for the cache descriptors
;
; cachesegD points to the first CACHETRACK descriptor
AX = number_ctsD
CX = CACHETRACK
MUL CX
; ax has size of CACHETRACK descriptors
AX += 15
CX = 16
DIV CX
; ax has descriptor size in paras
AX += 2
BX = AX
DO
   IF (umbs <> 0)
      aloc_umb(BX) ; allocate in paras
      IF (C) ; ok
         BX = cachesegD
         cachesegD = AX
         umbs = 1
         EXIT
      ENDIF
   ENDIF
   ; failed with umbs - use conv
   AX = cachesegD ; seg of descriptors
   BX += AX ; seg of cache
END
; BX has free para

; we also need a temporary track if we are not using conventional memory
tracksegD = 0
DO
   EXIT (memorytype <> EXTENDED && memorytype <> EXPANDED)
   ;
   AX = max_bpsD
   CX = max_sptD
   MUL CX
   CX = 16
   DIV CX
   ; ax has length of temp track in paras
   AX += 2
   ;
   ; try for the umbs again
   IF (umbs <> 0)
      PUSH AX
      aloc_umb(AX) ; in paras
      IF (C)
         ; ok
         tracksegD = AX
         umbs += 2
         EXIT
      ENDIF
      POP AX
   ENDIF
   ; failed - use conv
   tracksegD = BX
   BX += AX
END

; clear the CACHETRACK descriptors
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
XOR DI,DI
AX = number_ctsD
CX = CACHETRACK
MUL CX
CX = AX
XOR AX,AX
STOS BIR

; alocate the CT segments and put them into the CT descriptors
DO
   AL = memorytype
   IF (AL = CONVENTIONAL)
      memaloc_conv(BX) ; returns AX with free seg
      IF (NC)
         ; error in memory allocation
         displayline(&errorincmemaloc,1)
         CLC
      ENDIF
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = EXTENDED)
      memaloc_extended(BX)
      IF (NC)
         ; error in memory allocation
         displayline(&errorinxmemaloc,1)
         CLC
      ENDIF
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = EXPANDED)
      memaloc_expanded(BX)
      IF (NC)
         ; error in memory allocation
         displayline(&errorinememaloc,1)
         CLC
      ENDIF
      EXIT
   ENDIF
END
IF (NC)
   AX = 4C01H
   INT 21H
ENDIF
BX = AX


PUSH BX
; grab the INT13
AX = 3513H
INT 21H
normINT13.0.D = BX
normINT13.2.D = ES
PUSH DS
DX = &myINT13
AX = CS
DS = AX
AX = 2513H
INT 21H
POP DS

POP BX ; first free para
PUSH BX
showinstalled(BX)
check386()
cacheoff = 0
IF (disable = 1)
   ; disable on start up
   cacheoff = 1
ENDIF
AX = max_sptD
IF (readahead >= AL)
   readahead = 0
   restoftrack = 1
ENDIF

;#IF DEBUG
;LABEL testread
;AX = CS
;ES = AX
;BX = &testsector
;CX = 1
;DL = 0
;DH = 0
;AX = 0201H
;INT 13H
;#ENDIF

; TSR
POP BX ; seg of end of our memory
AX = BX
AX += 10
BX = pspD
DX = AX - BX
AX = 3100H
INT 21H             ;terminate but stay resident.

}
;------------------------
memaloc_conv (convfreesegD)
WORD
{
SAVE BX,CX,DX

; now intialise the CTs
BX = convfreesegD
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
DI = 0 ; LRU CT
ct_lruD = DI
CX = number_ctsD
SI = 0FFFFH
DO
   XOR AX,AX
   ES.DI.CTlruD.D = SI
   ES.DI.CTsegD.D = BX
   ES.DI.CTfsector = AL
   ES.DI.CTsectors = AL
   ES.DI.CTlocked = AL
   ES.DI.CTlastop = AL
   SI = DI
   DI += CACHETRACK
   BX += ct_lengthinparasD
   ES.SI.CTmruD.D = DI
   LOOP
   ES.SI.CTmruD.D = 0FFFFH
   ct_mruD = SI
END
; BX has and of our memory
AX = BX
STC
}
;------------------------
memaloc_extended (extfreesegD)
WORD
{
SAVE BX,CX,DX

; allocate the memory
aloc_ext(requestedKD)
IF (AX = 0)
   ; error
   CLC
   RETURN
ENDIF
xmmhandleD = AX

; CTsegD will have an half-kilobyte offset into the XMM block
AX = ct_lengthD
XOR DX,DX
CX = 512
DIV CX
DX = AX ; number halfK blocks in one CT

; now intialise the CTs
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
DI = 0 ; LRU CT
ct_lruD = DI
CX = number_ctsD
SI = 0FFFFH
BX = 0 ; offset into XMM block
DO
   ES.DI.CTlruD.D = SI
   ES.DI.CTsegD.D = BX
   XOR AX,AX
   ES.DI.CTfsector = AL
   ES.DI.CTsectors = AL
   ES.DI.CTlocked = AL
   ES.DI.CTlastop = AL
   SI = DI
   DI += CACHETRACK
   ES.SI.CTmruD.D = DI
   BX += DX ; next CT in halfK blocks
   LOOP
   ES.SI.CTmruD.D = 0FFFFH
   ct_mruD = SI
END
AX = extfreesegD
STC
}
;------------------------
memaloc_expanded (expfreesegD)
WORD
{
SAVE BX,CX,DX

; allocate the memory
aloc_exp(requestedKD)
IF (AX = 0)
   ; error
   CLC
   RETURN
ENDIF
emmhandleD = AX

; CTsegD will have an half-kilobyte offset into the EMM block
AX = ct_lengthD
XOR DX,DX
CX = 512
DIV CX
DX = AX ; number halfK blocks in one CT

; now intialise the CTs
AX = cachesegD
ES = AX
DI = 0 ; LRU CT
ct_lruD = DI
CX = number_ctsD
SI = 0FFFFH
BX = 0 ; offset into XMM block
DO
   ES.DI.CTlruD.D = SI
   ES.DI.CTsegD.D = BX
   XOR AX,AX
   ES.DI.CTfsector = AL
   ES.DI.CTsectors = AL
   ES.DI.CTlocked = AL
   ES.DI.CTlastop = AL
   SI = DI
   DI += CACHETRACK
   ES.SI.CTmruD.D = DI
   BX += DX ; next CT in halfK blocks
   LOOP
   ES.SI.CTmruD.D = 0FFFFH
   ct_mruD = SI
END
AX = expfreesegD
STC
}
;------------------------
aloc_exp(alockD)
WORD
{
; allocate memory from EMM and return handle in AX with C
; else NC
SAVE BX,CX,DX,SI,DI,ES
AX = alockD ; in K
CX = 16
XOR DX,DX
DIV CX
IF (DX <> 0)
   AX++
ENDIF
BX = AX ; in 16K pages
AH = 43H
INT 67H
IF (AH = 0)
   AX = DX
   STC
ELSE
   XOR AX,AX
   CLC
ENDIF

}
;------------------------
aloc_ext(alockD)
WORD
{
; allocate memory and return handle in AX
; and C else NC
SAVE BX,CX,DX,SI,DI,ES
DX = alockD ; K we require
AH = 9
AL = 0
CALL DWORD PTR xms
IF (AX = 1)
   AX = DX
   STC
ELSE
   XOR AX,AX
   CLC
ENDIF
}
;------------------------
aloc_umb(alockD)
WORD
{
; allocate UMB block and return segment in AX and C
; else NC and if no umbs AX =0FFFFH, or AX = avail paras
SAVE BX,CX,DX,SI,DI,ES
; size in paras
; ax has number paras
SI = alockD

AX = 5802H
INT 21H
linkflag = AL
AX = 5800H
INT 21H
strategyD = AX
XOR DI,DI
DO
   AX = 5803H
   BX = 1
   INT 21H
   EXIT (C)
   AX = 5801H
   BX = 40H
   INT 21H
   EXIT (C)
   DI++
   AX = 4800H
   BX = SI
   INT 21H
   EXIT (NC)
   AX = BX
END
PUSHF
PUSH AX
AX = 5803H
BL = linkflag
BH = 0
INT 21H
BX = strategyD
AX = 5801H
INT 21H

IF (DI = 0)
   POP AX
   POPF
   AX = 0FFFFH
   CLC
ELSE
   POP AX
   POPF
   CMC
ENDIF

}
;------------------------
check_memory ()
{
; check the memory type
DO
   IFL (memorytype = EXTENDED || memorytype = 0)
      ; see if XMM exists
      AX = 4300H
      INT 2FH
      IF (AL = 80H)
         ; exists
         ; get XMS
         AX = 4310H
         INT 2FH
         xms.0.D = BX
         xms.2.D = ES
         ; see how much exists
         AH = 08H
         CALL DWORD PTR xms
         ; dx has free X in K, ax has largest available block
         BX = AX
         IF (requestedKD = 0)
            SHR BX,1
         ENDIF
         IF (BX >= requestedKD && BX >= 64)
            ; we will use Xmem
            memorytype = EXTENDED
            IF (requestedKD = 0)
               requestedKD = BX
            ENDIF
            EXITL
         ENDIF
         ; insuf mem
         IF (memorytype = EXTENDED)
            IF (BX >= 64)
               requestedKD = BX
               memorytype = EXTENDED
               EXITL
            ENDIF
            displayline(&insufmem,1)
            CLC
            RETURN
         ENDIF
         ; try others
      ENDIF
      IF (memorytype = EXTENDED)
         displayline(&xmmnotexist,1)
         CLC
         RETURN
      ENDIF
   ENDIF
   IFL (memorytype = EXPANDED || memorytype = 0)
      ; see if EMM exists and status and version
      checkemm() ; rets AL: (0 - not exists,1 - not ready,2 - wrong version)
      IF (C)
         ; exists
         ; get page segment
         AH = 41H
         INT 67H
         emmsegD = BX
         ; see how much exists
         AH = 42H
         INT 67H
         ; bx has free 16K pages
         AX = BX
         CX = 16
         MUL CX
         BX = AX
         IF (requestedKD = 0)
            SHR BX,1
         ENDIF
         IF (BX >= requestedKD && BX >= 64)
            ; we will use Emem
            memorytype = EXPANDED
            IF (requestedKD = 0)
               requestedKD = BX
            ENDIF
            EXITL
         ENDIF
         ; insuf mem
         IF (memorytype = EXPANDED)
            IF (BX >= 64)
               requestedKD = BX
               memorytype = EXPANDED
               EXITL
            ENDIF
            displayline(&insufmem,1)
            CLC
            RETURN
         ENDIF
         ; try others
      ENDIF
      IF (memorytype = EXPANDED)
         IF (AL = 2)
            displayline(&emmwrong,1)
         ELSE
            displayline(&emmnotexist,1)
         ENDIF
         CLC
         RETURN
      ENDIF
   ENDIF
   IF (memorytype = CONVENTIONAL || memorytype = 0)
      ; See how much memory we have
      memorytype = CONVENTIONAL
      AX = pspD
      ES = AX
      BX = ES.2.D ; last segment of memory
      BX -= pspD
      ; minus the amount of code we have
;      AX = &endofcode
      AX = &init_data
      AX += 15
      CX = 16
      XOR DX,DX
      DIV CX
      ; paras of code
      CX = CS
      AX += CX
      AX -= pspD
      BX -= AX
      ; bx = number paragraphs available
      ; minus 64K for dos and 9K for our temporary track
      BX -= 4672
      IF (requestedKD = 0)
         SHR BX,1 ; take a half
      ENDIF
      ; convert to K
      AX = BX
      XOR DX,DX
      CX = 64
      DIV CX
      BX = AX
      IF (BX >= requestedKD && BX >= 64)
         IF (requestedKD = 0)
            requestedKD = BX
         ENDIF
         EXIT
      ENDIF
      ; insufficent memory
      IF (BX < 64) ; 64K in paras
         displayline(&insufmem,1)
         CLC
         RETURN
      ENDIF
      ; take it all
      requestedKD = BX;
   ENDIF
END
; the memory we will use is in memorytype
STC
}
;------------------------
checkemm ()
{
; Check for EMM and return C if all ok
; else NC and AL: (0-not exists, 1-bad status, 2-wrong version)
SAVE CX,SI,DI,ES

XOR AX,AX
ES = AX
DI = 019CH ; int 67h
AX = ES.DI.2.D
ES = AX
DI = 10
SI = &emmname
CX = 8
CLD
REPZ CMPSB
IF (NZ)
   AL = 0
   CLC
   RETURN
ENDIF
; check status
AH = 40H
INT 67H
IF (AH <> 0)
   AL = 1
   CLC
   RETURN
ENDIF
; check version
AH = 46H
INT 67H
IF (AH <> 0 || AL < 32H)
   AL = 2
   CLC
   RETURN
ENDIF
STC
}
;------------------------
check386()
{
; checks if the processor is a 386 and
; set the is386 flag accordingly

SAVE AX,BX,CX

PUSHF ; save flags
POP AX ; put into ax
BX = AX ; save
AND BX,4000H ; zero all but bit 14
XOR AX,4000H ; toggle NT bit (bit 14)
PUSH AX ; push new value
POPF ; into flags
PUSHF ; push flags
POP AX ; into ax
CX = AX ; get value
AND CX,4000H ; toggle all but bit 14
XOR AX,4000H ; toggle bit 14
PUSH AX ; push new value
POPF ; into flags
AL = 1 ; assume 386
IF (BX = CX)
   ; not a 386
   AL = 0
ENDIF
is386 = AL
}
;------------------------
build_drive_table()
{

; the BIOS call INT 13 (8):
;
;  Call:
;   AH = 8
;   DL = drive
;
;  Returns:
;   AH = 0 or error code
;   AL = 0
;   BH = 0
;   BL = drive type (0=none,1=no change,2=change,3=hard)
;   CH = low 8 bits of max tracks
;   CL = (0-5) max spt
;        (6-7) track
;   DH = max heads
;   DL = number drives installed
;   ES:DI points to floppy DBT

; now get the maximum possible bps and cpt
; use the INT13 (8) call to get info on drives
AH = 8
DL = 0
INT 13H
CL = ES.DI.3
AX = 128
SHL AX,CL
max_bpsD = AX
AL = ES.DI.4
AH = 0
max_sptD = AX
;
; a hard disk has 512 byte sectors, and its spt is added to max_sptD
; when we examine it below (INT13 (8) returns no DBT in ES:DI for a hard
; disk, so the old code here just re-read the floppy DBT and a hard disk
; with more spt than the floppy overran its CT)
IF (drive >= 80H)
   IF (max_bpsD < 512)
      max_bpsD = 512
   ENDIF
ENDIF

; clear the drivetable
DI = &drivetable
SI = DI
CX = DRIVEDEF*4
PUSH DS
POP ES
XOR AX,AX
STOS BIR

; examine the four drives
CL = 0
REPEAT
   IF (CL = 0 && drive = 0)
      ; for a floppy we must set the spt and bps on reading the 1st sector
      SI.DRVid = 0H
      SI.DRVtype = 2
      SI.DRVspt = 8 ; for 5 1/4 floppys
      SI.DRVheads = 2
      AX = max_bpsD
      SI.DRVbpsD.D = AX
   ENDIF
   IF (CL = 1 && drive = 1)
      ; for a floppy we must set the spt and bps on reading the 1st sector
      SI.DRVid = 01H
      SI.DRVtype = 2
      SI.DRVspt = 8 ; every floppy format has at least 8
      SI.DRVheads = 2
      AX = max_bpsD
      SI.DRVbpsD.D = AX
   ENDIF
   IF (CL = 2 && drive = 80H)
      ; for a hard disk we must examine the boot sector
      get_disk_info(drive) ; rets spt in AL and heads in AH
      EXIT (NC)
      update_max_spt()
      SI.DRVspt = AL
      SI.DRVheads = AH
      SI.DRVid = 80H
      SI.DRVtype = 3
      AX = max_bpsD
      SI.DRVbpsD.D = AX
   ENDIF
   IF (CL = 3 && drive = 81H)
      ; for a hard disk we must examine the boot sector
      get_disk_info(drive) ; rets spt in AL and heads in AH
      EXIT (NC)
      update_max_spt()
      SI.DRVspt = AL
      SI.DRVheads = AH
      SI.DRVid = 81H
      SI.DRVtype = 3
      AX = max_bpsD
      SI.DRVbpsD.D = AX
   ENDIF
   SI += DRIVEDEF
   INC CL
   IF (CL = 4)
      STC
      EXIT
   ENDIF
ENDREPL

}
;------------------------
get_disk_info (gdrive)
BYTE
{
; load up the boot sector for the disk
SAVE BX,CX,DX,DI,SI

; see if we are to use huge partitions
SI = 0
IF (dosversionD >= 0400H)
   ; calculate the size of the disk for BIGDOS
   DL = dosdrive
   DL++
   AH = 36H
   INT 21H
   PUSH DX
   MUL CX
   POP CX
   MUL CX
   IF (DX >= 512)
      SI = 1
   ENDIF
ENDIF

DI = 3
DO
   IF (SI = 0)
      CX = 1
      DX = 0
      BX = &bootsector
   ELSE
      CX = 0FFFFH
      BX = &hugetable
      XOR AX,AX
      BX.0.D = AX
      BX.2.D = AX
      BX.4.D = 1
      BX.6.D = &bootsector
      AX = DS
      BX.8.D = AX
   ENDIF
   AL = dosdrive
   PUSH SI
   PUSH DI
   INT 25H
   IF (C)
      POPF
      POP DI
      POP SI
      DI--
      CONTINUE (DI <> 0)
      XOR AX,AX
      CLC
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   POPF
   POP DI
   POP SI
   ; the drive is there, now get its geometry from the BIOS: we split
   ; INT13 requests into tracks with it, so it must be the BIOS's
   ; geometry for this BIOS drive, not what the BPB says
   PUSH ES
   AH = 8
   DL = gdrive
   INT 13H
   POP ES
   IF (C)
      XOR AX,AX
      CLC
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   AL = CL
   AND AL,00111111B ; spt
   AH = DH
   AH++ ; heads
   STC
END

}
;------------------------
update_max_spt ()
{
; make sure a CT can hold a track of AL sectors
PUSH AX
AH = 0
IF (AX > max_sptD)
   max_sptD = AX
ENDIF
POP AX
}
;------------------------
show_measurements (cachesizeD,msegD,moffD,mtype)
WORD
WORD
WORD
BYTE
{
; display the measurement data

JMP measurestart

MESSAGE cachemeas = 'Cache measurements:'
MESSAGE logtrans = '  Logical transfers  = '
MESSAGE phytrans = '  Physical transfers = '
MESSAGE savtrans = '  Transfers saved    = '
MESSAGE persaved = '  Percentage saved   = '

MESSAGE twospaces = '  '
MESSAGE memorymeas = 'Memory measurements:'
MESSAGE mcsize = 'K cache in '
MESSAGE mcon = 'K conventional memory used'

LABEL measurestart

displayline(&cachemeas,1)
;
AX = msegD
ES = AX
DI = moffD
;
; translate the logical transfers
displayline(&logtrans,0)
SI = &dnumber
AX = ES.DI.0.D
DX = ES.DI.2.D
dword2asc(SI,AX,DX)
displayline(SI,1)
;
; translate the physical transfers
displayline(&phytrans,0)
SI = &dnumber
AX = ES.DI.4.D
DX = ES.DI.6.D
dword2asc(SI,AX,DX)
displayline(SI,1)
;
; translate the saved transfers
displayline(&savtrans,0)
SI = &dnumber
; perform the subtraction
AX = ES.DI.0.D
DX = ES.DI.2.D
CX = ES.DI.6.D
AX -= ES.DI.4.D
IF (C)
   INC CX
ENDIF
DX -= CX
IF (C)
   XOR AX,AX
   DX = AX
ENDIF
PUSH AX
PUSH DX
dword2asc(SI,AX,DX)
displayline(SI,1)
;
; translate saved percent
displayline(&persaved,0)
POP DX ; number transfers saved * 100 / number logicals transfers
POP AX
calc_percent(DX,AX,ES.DI.2.D,ES.DI.0.D)
; rets in AX
SI = &dnumber
SI++
num2asc(SI,AX)
SI--
SI.0 = AL
AH = 0
PUSH SI
INC SI
SI += AX
SI.0 = '%'
SI.1 = 0
POP SI
SI.0 += 2
displayline(SI,1)
;
;
; now do the memory
DI += 8
displayNL()
displayline(&memorymeas,1)
displayline(&twospaces,0)
; size of cache
SI = &dnumber
SI++
num2asc(SI,cachesizeD)
SI--
SI.0 = AL
displayline(SI,0)
displayline(&mcsize,0)
DO
   IF (mtype = EXTENDED)
      SI = &ext_t
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (mtype = EXPANDED)
      SI = &exp_t
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   SI = &con_t
END
displayline(SI,1)
;
; convention memory used?
displayline(&twospaces,0)
SI = &dnumber
SI++
AX = ES.DI.0.D
num2asc(SI,AX)
SI--
SI.0 = AL
displayline(SI,0)
displayline(&mcon,1)
;
}
;------------------------
calc_percent (cp1D,cp2D,cp3D,cp4D)
WORD
WORD
WORD
WORD
{
; calculate percent: cp1:cp2 * 100 / cp2:cp4

SAVE DI

shld(6,cp1D,cp2D) ; * 64
BX = AX
CX = DX

shld(5,cp1D,cp2D)
BX += AX
IF (C)
   DX++
ENDIF
CX += DX

shld(2,cp1D,cp2D)
BX += AX
IF (C)
   DX++
ENDIF
CX += DX

; dx:ax has *100
doubleworddivide(CX,BX,cp3D,cp4D)

; has percentage in AX
}
;------------------------
shld (splaces,sd1D,sd2D)
BYTE
WORD
WORD
{
; shift the double word in sd1:sd2 by splaces
PUSH CX

AX = sd2D
DX = sd1D
CL = splaces
CH = 0
DO
   EXIT (CL = 0)
   SHL AX,1
   PUSHF
   SHL DX,1
   POPF
   IF (C)
      OR DX,1
   ENDIF
   LOOP
END
POP CX
}
;------------------------
doubleworddivide(valhD,vallD,byhD,bylD)
WORD
WORD
WORD
WORD
{
SAVE BX,CX,DX,DI,SI

BX = valhD
CX = vallD
DX = byhD
AX = bylD

DO
   IF (DX > BX || (DX = BX && AX > CX))
      AX = 0
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (BX = 0 && CX = 0)
      AX = 0
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (DX = BX && AX = CX)
      AX = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF

   DI = 0 ; counter
   REPEAT
      CX -= AX
      IF (C)
         SUB BX,1
         IF (C) ; possiblility of rounding
            CX += AX
            SHR CX,1
            IF (CX >= AX)
               DI++
            ENDIF
            EXIT
         ENDIF
      ENDIF
      BX -= DX
      IF (C)
         BX += DX
         TEST CX,8000H ; is top bit set (negative)
         IF (NZ)
            BX++
         ENDIF
         IF (BX = DX)
            SHR CX,1
            IF (CX >= AX)
               DI++
            ENDIF
         ENDIF
         EXIT
      ENDIF
      DI++
   ENDREP
   AX = DI
END
}
;-------------------------
showinstalled (ffparaD)
WORD
{

; where is cache
displayline(&cacheisin,0)
AL = memorytype
DO
   IF (AL = CONVENTIONAL)
      BX = &con_t
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = EXTENDED)
      BX = &ext_t
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = EXPANDED)
      BX = &exp_t
      EXIT
   ENDIF
END
displayline(BX,1)
displayNL()

; work out how much memory we have used
displayline(&codeused,0)
AX = ffparaD
AX -= pspD
CX = 64
XOR DX,DX
DIV CX
; ax has mem in K
IF (DX <> 0)
   AX++
ENDIF
DX = AX
convusedD = AX
SI = &dnumber
SI++
num2asc(SI,DX)
SI--
SI.0 = AL
displayline(SI,0)
displayline(&ink,1)

; see how much cache there is
displayline(&mcacheused,0)
AX = max_bpsD
CX = max_sptD
MUL CX
CX = number_ctsD
MUL CX
CX = 1024
DIV CX
; ax has K of cache
requestedKD = AX
DX = AX
SI = &dnumber
SI++
num2asc(SI,DX)
SI--
SI.0 = AL
displayline(SI,0)
displayline(&ink,1)
displayNL()

displayline(&instld,0)
IF (disable = 1)
   ; but we are disabled
   displayline(&butdisabled,0)
ENDIF
displayNL()

}
;------------------------
dword2asc(dastrD,lowD,highD)
WORD
WORD
WORD
{
; do in two parts of 10,000
SAVE BX,CX,DX,SI

BX = lowD
DX = highD
SI = dastrD
SI.0 = 0
PUSH SI
SI++
CX = 10000
IF (DX <> 0 || BX >= CX)
   AX = BX
   DIV CX
   PUSH DX
   num2asc(SI,AX)
   SI--
   SI.0 = AL + 4
   SI++
   SI += AX
   PUSH SI
   CX = 5 - AX
   DO
      SI.0 = '0'
      SI++
      LOOP
   END
   POP SI
   POP BX
   XOR DX,DX
   DO
      IF (BX = 0 || BX < 10)
         SI += 3
         EXIT
      ENDIF
      IF (BX < 100)
         SI += 2
         EXIT
      ENDIF
      IF (BX < 1000)
         SI++
         EXIT
      ENDIF
   END
ENDIF

num2asc(SI,BX)
POP SI
IF (SI.0 = 0)
   SI.0 = AL
ENDIF
AL = SI.0
AH = 0

}
;------------------------
num2asc(nastrD,navalD)
WORD
WORD
{
; convert the word in navalD into an ASCIIZ string starting at nastrD
; returns length in AX
PUSH BX
PUSH CX
PUSH DX
PUSH SI
PUSH DI
DI = nastrD
AX = navalD
CX = 10
XOR BX,BX
REPEAT
   EXIT (AX = 0)
   XOR DX,DX
   DIV CX
   ; char is in DL
   DL += 48
   DI.0 = DL
   DI++
   BX++
ENDREP
; length is in BX
IF (BX = 0)
   DI.0 = '0'
   DI++
   BX++
ENDIF
PUSH BX
DI.0 = 0
CX = BX
SHR BX,1
IF (C)
   CX--
ENDIF
SHR CX,1
DI--
SI = nastrD
DO
   EXIT (CX = 0)
   AL = SI.0
   AH = DI.0
   SI.0 = AH
   DI.0 = AL
   SI++
   DI--
   LOOP
END
POP AX
POP DI
POP SI
POP DX
POP CX
POP BX
}
;------------------------
parseparameter(para)
BYTE
{
AL = para
DO
   EXITL (installed = 1)
   IF (AL = '?')
      uninstalledhelp()
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'X')
      memorytype = EXTENDED
      EXITL
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'E')
      memorytype = EXPANDED
      EXITL
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'C')
      memorytype = CONVENTIONAL
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'D')
      disable = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'H')
      hitindicator = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'A')
      allowredundant = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'M')
      minimise = 1
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'R')
      readpriority = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'T')
      AL = ES.SI.0
      SI++
      IF (AL = ':')
         ; point to number
         cl_asc2num()
         ; DX has value, AL has last char
         readahead = DL
         restoftrack = 0
         SI--
         EXIT
      ENDIF
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'U')
      uninstall = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   #IF DVERSION
   IF (AL = 'W')
      allowwrite = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   #ENDIF
   CLC
   RETURN
END
DO
   EXIT (installed = 0)
   IF (AL = '?')
      installedhelp()
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'D')
      disable = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'E')
      disable = 2 ; enable
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'F')
      rflush = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'O')
      showparas = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'M')
      showmeasures = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = 'U')
      uninstall = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   #IF DEBUG
   IF (AL = 'I')
      displaycache = 1
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   #ENDIF
   CLC
   RETURN
END
STC
}
;-------------------------
displayline (dlineD,dnl)
WORD
BYTE
{
SAVE BX,CX
BX = dlineD
CL = BX.0
CH = 0
BX++
DO
   EXIT (CL = 0)
   AL = BX.0
   BX++
   EXIT (AL = 0)
   displaychar(AL)
   LOOP
END
IF (dnl = 1)
   displayNL()
ENDIF
}
;------------------------
displaychar (dchar)
BYTE
{
PUSH BX
AH = 0EH
AL = dchar
INT 10H
POP BX
}
;------------------------
displayNL ()
{
displaychar(10)
displaychar(13)
}
;------------------------
uppercase ()
{
IF (AL >= 'a' && AL <= 'z')
   AL -= 'a'
   AL += 'A'
ENDIF
}
;------------------------
cl_asc2num ()
{
; convert ascii to number of command line
; return in DX, last char in AL

SAVE BX,CX

BX = 0
CX = 10
REPEAT
   AL = ES.SI.0
   SI++
   EXIT (AL = 32 || AL = 13)
   PUSH AX
   AX = BX
   MUL CX
   BX = AX
   POP AX
   AL -= '0'
   AH = 0
   BX += AX
ENDREP
DX = BX
}
;------------------------
getdisplaytype()
{
;find out what kind of display adaptor is being used
AH = 15 ;get video mode
INT 10H
IF (AL = 7) ;monochrome adapter mode
   AX = 0B000H
ELSE
   AX = 0B800H
ENDIF
displayparaD = AX
}
;------------------------
show_parameters(psegD,poffD,mtype)
WORD
WORD
BYTE
{
JMP sp_start

MESSAGE sp1 = 'Current options are:'
MESSAGE spa = '  Allow redundant writes:       '
MESSAGE sph = '  Hit indicator:                '
MESSAGE spm = '  Minimise conventional memory: '
MESSAGE spr = '  Read has priority over write: '
MESSAGE spt = '  Read-ahead sectors in track:  '
#IF DVERSION
MESSAGE spw = '  Allow writes (DEBUG version): '
#ENDIF

MESSAGE off = 'OFF'
MESSAGE on = 'ON'
MESSAGE all = 'ALL'

LABEL sp_start

AX = psegD
ES = AX
DI = poffD
; ES:DI point to:
;allowredundant
;hitindicator
;minimise
;readpriority
;restoftrack
;readahead

displayline(&sp1,1)
;
displayline(&spa,0)
AL = ES.DI.0
displayyesno(AL)
;
displayline(&sph,0)
AL = ES.DI.1
displayyesno(AL)
;
displayline(&spm,0)
AL = ES.DI.2
displayyesno(AL)
;
displayline(&spr,0)
AL = ES.DI.3
displayyesno(AL)
;
displayline(&spt,0)
CH = ES.DI.4
; restoftrack
CL = ES.DI.5
; readahead
DO
   IF (CH = 1)
      displayline(&all,1)
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (CL = 0)
      displayline(&off,1)
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   BX = &dnumber
   BX++
   num2asc(BX,CX)
   BX--
   BX.0 = AL
   displayline(BX,1)
END
;
#IF DVERSION
displayline(&spw,0)
AL = ES.DI.6
displayyesno(AL)
#ENDIF
;
displayNL()
displaychar(32)
displaychar(32)
displayline(&cacheisin,0)
AL = mtype
DO
   IF (AL = EXTENDED)
      BX = &ext_t
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   IF (AL = EXPANDED)
      BX = &exp_t
      EXIT
   ENDIF
   BX = &con_t
END
displayline(BX,1)
;
}
;------------------------
displayyesno(yesno)
BYTE
{
IF (yesno = 0)
   displayline(&off,1)
ELSE
   displayline(&on,1)
ENDIF
}
;------------------------
uninstalledhelp()
{
JMP uninhelp

MESSAGE uh1 = 'MI-CACHE has not been loaded. To load type MICACHE'
MESSAGE uh2 = 'Usage: MICACHE drive: [size] [options]'
MESSAGE uh3 = '  [size] is the size of the cache in kilobytes (KB)'
MESSAGE uh4 = '  [options] are:'
MESSAGE uhx = '    -X    Use extended memory for cache'
MESSAGE uhe = '    -E    Use expanded memory for cache'
MESSAGE uhc = '    -C    Use conventional memory for cache'
MESSAGE uha = '    -A    Allow redundant writes'
MESSAGE uhd = '    -D    Start up cache disabled'
MESSAGE uhh = '    -H    Show cache HIT indicator'
MESSAGE uhm = '    -M    Minimise use of conventional memory'
MESSAGE uhr = '    -R    Give read priority over writes'
MESSAGE uht = '    -T:nn Read nn sectors ahead in track (default is all)'
MESSAGE uhq = '    -?    Display this help screen'
#IF DVERSION
MESSAGE uhw = '    -w    Allow writes to disk (DEBUG version only)'
#ENDIF

LABEL uninhelp
displayline(&uh1,1)
displayNL()
displayline(&uh2,1)
displayNL()
displayline(&uh3,1)
displayNL()
displayline(&uh4,1)
displayline(&uhx,1)
displayline(&uhe,1)
displayline(&uhc,1)
displayNL()
displayline(&uha,1)
displayline(&uhd,1)
displayline(&uhh,1)
IF (dosversionD >= 0500H)
   displayline(&uhm,1)
ENDIF
displayline(&uhr,1)
displayline(&uht,1)
displayNL()
displayline(&uhq,1)
#IF DVERSION
displayline(&uhw,1)
#ELSE
displayNL()
#ENDIF

AX = 4C00H
INT 21H
}
;------------------------
installedhelp ()
{
JMP inhelp

MESSAGE ih1 = 'MI-CACHE is loaded'
MESSAGE ih2 = 'Usage: MICACHE [options]'
MESSAGE ih3 = '  [Options] are:'

MESSAGE ihd = '    -D    Disable caching'
MESSAGE ihe = '    -E    Enable caching'
MESSAGE ihf = '    -F    Flush cache'
MESSAGE ihm = '    -M    Display measurements'
MESSAGE iho = '    -O    Show options in use'
MESSAGE ihu = '    -U    Unload MICACHE from memory'
MESSAGE ihq = '    -?    Display this help screen'
#IF DEBUG
MESSAGE ihi = '    -I    Show cache info (DEBUG version)'
#ENDIF

LABEL inhelp

displayline(&ih1,0)
; get state of cache
AX = 0FF00H
CL = 'M'
CH = 'I'
DL = 0FFH
INT 13H
IF (AH = 1)
   ; disabled
   displayline(&butdisabled,0)
ENDIF
displayNL()
displayNL()

displayline(&ih2,1)
displayNL()
displayline(&ih3,1)
displayline(&ihd,1)
displayline(&ihe,1)
displayline(&ihf,1)
displayline(&ihm,1)
displayline(&iho,1)
displayline(&ihu,1)
displayline(&ihq,1)
#IF DEBUG
displayline(&ihi,1)
#ENDIF
displayNL()


AX = 4C00H
INT 21H
}
;------------------------
endofcode ()
{
}
